886
00:26:01.569 --> 00:26:03.418
And again, I thought I was gonna be the first one.

887
00:26:03.418 --> 00:26:04.251
I have no idea.

888
00:26:04.251 --> 00:26:05.211
Clueless.

889
00:26:05.211 --> 00:26:07.583
And she looked at me and she goes, "Oh no."

890
00:26:07.583 --> 00:26:09.228
'Cause she knows when I try to do something,

891
00:26:09.228 --> 00:26:11.086
now at that point, I have to do it.

892
00:26:11.086 --> 00:26:13.219
And her, she's like, all right,

893
00:26:13.219 --> 00:26:15.215
she started doing research for me.

894
00:26:15.215 --> 00:26:17.631
And then that's when we discovered Robbie Balenger.

895
00:26:17.631 --> 00:26:18.464
Right.

896
00:26:18.464 --> 00:26:21.070
And that's how the idea of running every day,

897
00:26:21.070 --> 00:26:23.670
running across the country came up after year two,

898
00:26:23.670 --> 00:26:25.908
when I said I needed run across the country.

899
00:26:25.908 --> 00:26:26.741
Right. All right.

900
00:26:26.741 --> 00:26:27.766
Well, we're gonna get into that in a second,

901
00:26:27.766 --> 00:26:30.732
but I have to ask, during this couple of years

902
00:26:30.732 --> 00:26:32.535
when you're running every single day,

903
00:26:32.535 --> 00:26:34.073
there's some travel in there too, right?

904
00:26:34.073 --> 00:26:35.282
Oh, yeah.

905
00:26:35.282 --> 00:26:36.395
Like you had to go to Australia,

906
00:26:36.395 --> 00:26:39.000
like how are you making sure that you're not missing a day?

907
00:26:39.000 --> 00:26:39.970
That day, yeah.

908
00:26:39.970 --> 00:26:41.337
There's some tricky moments in there,

909
00:26:41.337 --> 00:26:42.524
where it was touch and go,

910
00:26:42.524 --> 00:26:43.821
whether you were gonna able to squeeze it in.

911
00:26:43.821 --> 00:26:46.296
Yeah, so, so many times I've flown,

912
00:26:46.296 --> 00:26:48.254
I would get up 2:00 or 3:00 in the morning to run.

913
00:26:48.254 --> 00:26:50.514
So, I wanna be in control of what I can do.

914
00:26:50.514 --> 00:26:52.800
I don't wanna go to the airport, get stuck at the airport,

915
00:26:52.800 --> 00:26:55.495
or I don't have a mean to get out to run.

916
00:26:55.495 --> 00:26:56.837
So, I get up very early to run.

917
00:26:56.837 --> 00:26:59.663
So, they'll show the opportunity cam with GoPro.

918
00:26:59.663 --> 00:27:02.528
And I told GoPro, "No, I'm not going."

919
00:27:02.528 --> 00:27:03.423
To Australia.

920
00:27:03.423 --> 00:27:04.256
Right. Yeah.

921
00:27:04.256 --> 00:27:06.486
Yeah, and I said, "I'm so sorry this is great,

922
00:27:06.486 --> 00:27:07.447
but because of running, I-

923
00:27:07.447 --> 00:27:08.687
I can't break the streak.

924
00:27:08.687 --> 00:27:11.285
Yeah, because of running, I met you guys.

925
00:27:11.285 --> 00:27:12.379
It's very important to me to run.

926
00:27:12.379 --> 00:27:14.483
And to go to our show, it was like 27 hours.

927
00:27:14.483 --> 00:27:15.575
I'm gonna miss a day.

928
00:27:15.575 --> 00:27:17.894
So, they find a way to connect me with a travel agent.

929
00:27:17.894 --> 00:27:21.181
So, I set up the trip where I don't mess up my streak.

930
00:27:21.181 --> 00:27:24.362
