And because of the transcontinental,

984
00:29:05.833 --> 00:29:10.196
I averaged over eight miles a day for the whole four years.

985
00:29:10.196 --> 00:29:13.401
So, my favorite mile is going on a seven-mile run

986
00:29:13.401 --> 00:29:15.719
because something that kinda tests me, but doesn't break me.

987
00:29:15.719 --> 00:29:16.552
The sweet spot.

988
00:29:16.552 --> 00:29:17.385
Yeah, it's the sweet spot.

989
00:29:17.385 --> 00:29:18.311
Yeah, is that what you did today?

990
00:29:18.311 --> 00:29:19.144
Today no.

991
00:29:19.144 --> 00:29:19.977
I did five miles today.

992
00:29:19.977 --> 00:29:20.810
Okay.

993
00:29:20.810 --> 00:29:21.643
All right, maybe you have to get out

994
00:29:21.643 --> 00:29:22.476
and do two more.

995
00:29:22.476 --> 00:29:23.309
Yeah, two more.

996
00:29:23.309 --> 00:29:24.142
We can go out right now.

997
00:29:24.142 --> 00:29:24.975
Do you have your shoes? (laughs)

998
00:29:24.975 --> 00:29:25.808
(laughs) I might have my car.

999
00:29:25.808 --> 00:29:27.445
Yeah. (laughs)

1000
00:29:27.445 --> 00:29:28.278
Cool.

1001
00:29:28.278 --> 00:29:30.680
So, the idea for the transcontinental run

1002
00:29:30.680 --> 00:29:32.926
comes into your awareness,

1003
00:29:32.926 --> 00:29:36.416
a great opportunity to make this about something broader

1004
00:29:36.416 --> 00:29:37.996
than just maintaining a streak.

1005
00:29:37.996 --> 00:29:39.267
A streak. Exactly.

1006
00:29:39.267 --> 00:29:41.380
How did you become aware of Robbie?

1007
00:29:41.380 --> 00:29:44.040
So, again, Belle, I'm telling you without her,

1008
00:29:44.040 --> 00:29:45.329
I wouldn't even be probably sitting here

1009
00:29:45.329 --> 00:29:47.097
