I lost. (laughs)

1309
00:39:18.179 --> 00:39:19.534
In those early videos, you're like,

1310
00:39:19.534 --> 00:39:21.235
this is a soccer player.

1311
00:39:21.235 --> 00:39:22.176
A soccer player, buddy.

1312
00:39:22.176 --> 00:39:24.997
With stubby legs and the whole thing.

1313
00:39:24.997 --> 00:39:27.228
It's amazing to see the body transformation.

1314
00:39:27.228 --> 00:39:28.061
Everything changed.

1315
00:39:28.061 --> 00:39:30.691
And just the natural kind of stride that you have.

1316
00:39:30.691 --> 00:39:31.961
You're like, "That guy looks like he knows how to run."

1317
00:39:31.961 --> 00:39:33.469
Yeah, everything changed.

1318
00:39:33.469 --> 00:39:35.637
And that goes in with time too.

1319
00:39:35.637 --> 00:39:37.702
So, I tell people if you're getting into running,

1320
00:39:37.702 --> 00:39:38.599
it's gonna eventually change.

1321
00:39:38.599 --> 00:39:40.021
Just stay consistent with it.

1322
00:39:40.021 --> 00:39:40.854
Yeah.

1323
00:39:40.854 --> 00:39:41.687
Yeah, everything changed.

1324
00:39:41.687 --> 00:39:44.614
Losing the weight is just gonna happen.

1325
00:39:44.614 --> 00:39:46.882
You just gotta make sure you eat as much as you can.

1326
00:39:46.882 --> 00:39:48.104
And I remember actually last summer,

1327
00:39:48.104 --> 00:39:50.060
I was training for a 5k PR.

1328
00:39:50.060 --> 00:39:53.324
So, I lost weight just because just sweating a lot,

1329
00:39:53.324 --> 00:39:54.157
just naturally.

1330
00:39:54.157 --> 00:39:55.557
Didn't even plan on doing it.

1331
00:39:55.557 --> 00:39:59.241
And I remember someone on my YouTube channel actually,

1332
00:39:59.241 --> 00:40:02.639
who has like a 10,000-something streak day.

1333
00:40:02.639 --> 00:40:05.077
Yeah, he lives in Michigan.

1334
00:40:05.077 --> 00:40:06.359
I can't believe I'm blanking on his name now.

1335
00:40:06.359 --> 00:40:08.171
He's like a good friend of ours,

1336
00:40:08.171 --> 00:40:10.355
like on YouTube always commenting.

1337
00:40:10.355 --> 00:40:13.247
And he said, "Hellah, you have a race body now.

1338
00:40:13.247 --> 00:40:14.755
This is the race weight."

1339
00:40:14.755 --> 00:40:17.083
So, you just lose weight by just running.

1340
00:40:17.083 --> 00:40:18.023
Yeah.

1341
00:40:18.023 --> 00:40:21.915
So, the idea is to try to get this done in under a 100 days.

1342
00:40:21.915 --> 00:40:22.956
Yeah, that's the goal.

1343
00:40:22.956 --> 00:40:23.898
But secretly.

1344
00:40:23.898 --> 00:40:25.045
I wanted 85 days.

1345
00:40:25.045 --> 00:40:25.878
85.

1346
00:40:25.878 --> 00:40:26.711
Yeah.

1347
00:40:26.711 --> 00:40:27.544
You got it done in 84.

1348
00:40:27.544 --> 00:40:28.377
84, yeah.

1349
00:40:28.377 --> 00:40:30.416
Which means how many miles a day?

1350
00:40:30.416 --> 00:40:32.333
Just over 36 average.

1351
00:40:33.300 --> 00:40:36.262
But the crazy thing for me to think about it,

1352
00:40:36.262 --> 00:40:39.461
the first half to get to the first half of the country,

1353
00:40:39.461 --> 00:40:41.711
it took me almost 50 days.

1354
00:40:41.711 --> 00:40:44.012
The second half I did it in 34 days,

1355
00:40:44.012 --> 00:40:46.520
which show how much I had really had to go through

1356
00:40:46.520 --> 00:40:47.353
in the mountain.

1357
00:40:47.353 --> 00:40:50.197
The mountain areas really beat me up and slow me down.

1358
00:40:50.197 --> 00:40:51.485
I was talking to Robbie a lot.

1359
00:40:51.485 --> 00:40:54.378
And he said, "Hellah, my advantage was I lived in Colorado.

1360
00:40:54.378 --> 00:40:55.648
I was always running in the mountains."

1361
00:40:55.648 --> 00:40:58.632
I live in New Jersey, 92 feet above sea level.

1362
00:40:58.632 --> 00:41:00.882
My whole, almost three, four years of running every day,

1363
00:41:00.882 --> 00:41:04.390
my elevation gain I don't think total was more than 4,000.

1364
00:41:04.390 --> 00:41:05.223
Right.

1365
00:41:05.223 --> 00:41:06.110
All pavement and hills.

1366
00:41:06.110 --> 00:41:07.976
Yeah, and I call those hills massive speed bumps.

1367
00:41:07.976 --> 00:41:09.412
I don't think they're hills.

1368
00:41:09.412 --> 00:41:10.245
They're not at all.

1369
00:41:10.245 --> 00:41:11.415
(laughs) Yeah.

1370
00:41:11.415 --> 00:41:14.027
So, you went through this acclimation phase

1371
00:41:14.027 --> 00:41:15.289
of having to get fitter,

1372
00:41:15.289 --> 00:41:19.872
while also your body trying to get used to the pounding

1373
00:41:21.326 --> 00:41:23.759
and the vert and the different types of weather.

1374
00:41:23.759 --> 00:41:26.429
I know your feet like swelled up and all kinds of stuff.

1375
00:41:26.429 --> 00:41:27.683
You went from like a size 10 to 11 and a half.

1376
00:41:27.683 --> 00:41:29.593
To 11 and a half, yeah.

1377
00:41:29.593 --> 00:41:30.426
Wow, man.

1378
00:41:30.426 --> 00:41:33.324
Yeah, and the knee was swelled up,

1379
00:41:33.324 --> 00:41:36.724
ankle was swelled up and shins were flared,

1380
00:41:36.724 --> 00:41:38.170
blisters everywhere.

1381
00:41:38.170 --> 00:41:39.267
And the running in there.

1382
00:41:39.267 --> 00:41:40.388
And me, I went in,

1383
00:41:40.388 --> 00:41:41.695
Robbie warned me too.

1384
00:41:41.695 --> 00:41:42.778
I've had warnings.

1385
00:41:42.778 --> 00:41:45.480
And you kinda like, you learn your lessons.

1386
00:41:45.480 --> 00:41:47.885
He told me, "Hellah, get these sticks."

1387
00:41:47.885 --> 00:41:48.827
Checking sticks.

1388
00:41:48.827 --> 00:41:49.953
So, I was laughing and I was like-

1389
00:41:49.953 --> 00:41:50.786
Poles.

1390
00:41:50.786 --> 00:41:51.619
I said, poles, yeah.

1391
00:41:51.619 --> 00:41:53.191
I said, "Robbie, who needs a pole to run?"

1392
00:41:53.191 --> 00:41:55.192
'Cause we have like a comfortable relationship.

1393
00:41:55.192 --> 00:41:56.247
Like we joke around.

1394
00:41:56.247 --> 00:41:58.316
And he said, "Trust me, it's gonna make a huge difference."

1395
00:41:58.316 --> 00:42:00.126
So, I get them there with me,

1396
00:42:00.126 --> 00:42:01.840
then use it in California at all.

1397
00:42:01.840 --> 00:42:04.923
So, me being me, I was running up everything.

1398
00:42:04.923 --> 00:42:07.742
And I was listening to "Born to Run" in the beginning.

1399
00:42:07.742 --> 00:42:10.327
And it says in "Born to Run," for ultra racing,

1400
00:42:10.327 --> 00:42:13.139
if you don't see the top of the hill do not run it.

1401
00:42:13.139 --> 00:42:14.257
It is wasteful energy.

1402
00:42:14.257 --> 00:42:15.249
It's not gonna take you anywhere.

1403
00:42:15.249 --> 00:42:16.573
You think that down hills are gonna help at that point,

1404
00:42:16.573 --> 00:42:17.406
your legs are beat up.

1405
00:42:17.406 --> 00:42:18.753
You're not even making any progress.

1406
00:42:18.753 --> 00:42:21.085
So, I was running everything up.

1407
00:42:21.085 --> 00:42:24.728
That's when I messed up my knee and ankle became a problem.

1408
00:42:24.728 --> 00:42:26.845
And in my hip was so out of line,

1409
00:42:26.845 --> 00:42:29.280
it was like two inch above the other.

1410
00:42:29.280 --> 00:42:31.701
My right knee versus the left knee.

1411
00:42:31.701 --> 00:42:33.636
So, I had to really, I called Robbie.

1412
00:42:33.636 --> 00:42:35.598
I said, "How did you do this?"

1413
00:42:35.598 --> 00:42:36.453
He said, "What are you doing?"

1414
00:42:36.453 --> 00:42:37.651
I said, "Yeah, I'm running everything."

1415
00:42:37.651 --> 00:42:39.263
He said, "You're not supposed to be running everything,

1416
00:42:39.263 --> 00:42:40.137
Hellah.

1417
00:42:40.137 --> 00:42:41.799
You cannot run up these."

1418
00:42:41.799 --> 00:42:43.205
And then you're gaining.

1419
00:42:43.205 --> 00:42:44.459
At one of my run, I gained-

1420
00:42:44.459 --> 00:42:45.767
You're not going any faster anywhere.

1421
00:42:45.767 --> 00:42:46.600
You're not.

1422
00:42:46.600 --> 00:42:47.774
I'm literally slowing myself down.

1423
00:42:47.774 --> 00:42:49.700
So, I kinda like got into the ultra,

1424
00:42:49.700 --> 00:42:51.498
listening to "Born to Run,"

1425
00:42:51.498 --> 00:42:53.132
actually taking tips from then,

1426
00:42:53.132 --> 00:42:54.953
calling Robbie if I have any question.

1427
00:42:54.953 --> 00:42:57.238
And I got stronger as I was going.

1428
00:42:57.238 --> 00:43:00.056
Technique was changing, strategies were changing.

1429
00:43:00.056 --> 00:43:02.498
And that's why I had a better, stronger April month

1430
00:43:02.498 --> 00:43:03.555
compared to March,

1431
00:43:03.555 --> 00:43:07.388
where I basically went from 876 miles in March

1432
00:43:08.396 --> 00:43:12.434
to 1,225 miles in April with one day less.

1433
00:43:12.434 --> 00:43:15.167
And even the elevation gain was worse in April

1434
00:43:15.167 --> 00:43:16.342
compared to March.

1435
00:43:16.342 --> 00:43:18.764
It's amazing how the body can just get used to that.

1436
00:43:18.764 --> 00:43:19.597
Yeah, figure that.

1437
00:43:19.597 --> 00:43:20.808
Figure it out like originally,

1438
00:43:20.808 --> 00:43:23.069
you're having all these problems 'cause it's like,

1439
00:43:23.069 --> 00:43:24.191
"What are you doing to me?"

1440
00:43:24.191 --> 00:43:25.024
Yeah, exactly.

1441
00:43:25.024 --> 00:43:25.857
Right?

1442
00:43:25.857 --> 00:43:27.674
You make a few tweaks, you keep going,

1443
00:43:27.674 --> 00:43:28.957
and suddenly those things get resolved and-

1444
00:43:28.957 --> 00:43:31.776
It all comes together perfectly, yeah.

1445
00:43:31.776 --> 00:43:34.835
So, throughout that whole experience,

1446
00:43:34.835 --> 00:43:37.209
I mean, hit me with some of the highlights.

1447
00:43:37.209 --> 00:43:39.230
Yeah, the best is like going through

1448
00:43:39.230 --> 00:43:42.375
the Navajo reservation in New Mexico was incredible.

1449
00:43:42.375 --> 00:43:43.650
So, the message travel.

1450
00:43:43.650 --> 00:43:45.307
If I meet somebody,

1451
00:43:45.307 --> 00:43:46.539
by the time I get to a different part of the reservation,

1452
00:43:46.539 --> 00:43:48.219
they already know I'm coming

1453
00:43:48.219 --> 00:43:49.510
because someone will say something.

1454
00:43:49.510 --> 00:43:50.343
They're all talking, yeah.

1455
00:43:50.343 --> 00:43:51.761
And people getting ready for gifts.

1456
00:43:51.761 --> 00:43:54.742
Someone has made me a necklace,

1457
00:43:54.742 --> 00:43:55.855
that we're getting feathers,

1458
00:43:55.855 --> 00:43:58.948
has a gift like telling us what the meaning behind it,

1459
00:43:58.948 --> 00:43:59.852
key chain.

1460
00:43:59.852 --> 00:44:01.272
And even Belle got a gift.

1461
00:44:01.272 --> 00:44:02.733
Garrett got a gift.

1462
00:44:02.733 --> 00:44:06.552
So, and I met the first person to come and run with me

1463
00:44:06.552 --> 00:44:08.902
was Zack from the Navajo reservation.

1464
00:44:08.902 --> 00:44:09.942
He was a native.

1465
00:44:09.942 --> 00:44:12.970
And he came when Robbie came the same day.

1466
00:44:12.970 --> 00:44:13.803
Oh, wow.

1467
00:44:13.803 --> 00:44:14.636
So, he said, "Can I run with you, Hellah?"

1468
00:44:14.636 --> 00:44:15.469
I said, "Yeah, of course."

1469
00:44:15.469 --> 00:44:17.749
So, we ran 15 miles together that day.

1470
00:44:17.749 --> 00:44:19.056
And then he said, "Can I get your number?"

1471
00:44:19.056 --> 00:44:20.581
And I said, "Yeah, sure."

1472
00:44:20.581 --> 00:44:22.389
So, he texted me and said, "Can I get your location?

1473
00:44:22.389 --> 00:44:23.222
I wanna come back again."

1474
00:44:23.222 --> 00:44:26.398
He came back the next day and ran 30 miles with me.

1475
00:44:26.398 --> 00:44:27.428
So, that was really cool.

1476
00:44:27.428 --> 00:44:29.521
That's when people started coming in at that point.

1477
00:44:29.521 --> 00:44:31.552
And it was just incredible.

1478
00:44:31.552 --> 00:44:35.598
Just like the beauty of the reservation,

1479
00:44:35.598 --> 00:44:36.869
New Mexico and the people itself,

1480
00:44:36.869 --> 00:44:38.983
that was one of the biggest highlights.

1481
00:44:38.983 --> 00:44:40.135
Yeah.

1482
00:44:40.135 --> 00:44:41.279
Do you have to,

1483
00:44:41.279 --> 00:44:42.407
I remember talking to Robbie

1484
00:44:42.407 --> 00:44:43.763
about going through the Navajo Nation.

1485
00:44:43.763 --> 00:44:45.534
I mean, it can be tricky, right?

1486
00:44:45.534 --> 00:44:46.367
Yeah.

1487
00:44:46.367 --> 00:44:47.769
Like it's not just a free fall.

1488
00:44:47.769 --> 00:44:49.589
Like do you have to alert them ahead of time?

1489
00:44:49.589 --> 00:44:51.724
Like, "Hey, we're coming, is it cool for mission?"

1490
00:44:51.724 --> 00:44:53.484
Certain areas, yeah.

1491
00:44:53.484 --> 00:44:54.818
Just sort of shake the hands

1492
00:44:54.818 --> 00:44:57.332
and make sure that sort of-

1493
00:44:57.332 --> 00:44:59.238
Yeah, we didn't have to deal with that much,

1494
00:44:59.238 --> 00:45:01.769
but there was one time that a lady stopped us

1495
00:45:01.769 --> 00:45:03.614
and told me, "You gotta wear a vest.

1496
00:45:03.614 --> 00:45:05.527
You can't be running on the roads without wearing a vest."

1497
00:45:05.527 --> 00:45:08.634
I only would put on my kind of safety vests at night-

1498
00:45:08.634 --> 00:45:09.551
Reflective, yeah.

1499
00:45:09.551 --> 00:45:11.896
Reflective vest at night, so I can be seen by cars.

1500
00:45:11.896 --> 00:45:14.687
But during the day, she's like, "You gotta put this on."

1501
00:45:14.687 --> 00:45:17.987
And she explained to me about people drinking and driving,

1502
00:45:17.987 --> 00:45:19.233
you don't wanna get hit.

1503
00:45:19.233 --> 00:45:21.177
And she was like, "You have no choice."

1504
00:45:21.177 --> 00:45:22.899
Like she's like, "Do this now."

1505
00:45:22.899 --> 00:45:24.854
So, with respect also, I'm like, "Well, it won't hurt me.

1506
00:45:24.854 --> 00:45:26.645
It's just extra safety."

1507
00:45:26.645 --> 00:45:28.023
So, we put it on.

1508
00:45:28.023 --> 00:45:29.325
But there's been areas

1509
00:45:29.325 --> 00:45:32.340
where we've got invited to used people's land

1510
00:45:32.340 --> 00:45:34.079
to have RV park overnight.

1511
00:45:34.079 --> 00:45:36.441
Yeah, because there's nowhere to park.

1512
00:45:36.441 --> 00:45:37.274
It's not safe.

1513
00:45:37.274 --> 00:45:39.450
And then those are open land that people owned.

1514
00:45:39.450 --> 00:45:41.484
So, they're like we had a gentleman say,

1515
00:45:41.484 --> 00:45:42.710
"Hey, can you come in?

1516
00:45:42.710 --> 00:45:44.008
You can come and park your RV overnight

1517
00:45:44.008 --> 00:45:45.811
'cause I have no use of that space.

1518
00:45:45.811 --> 00:45:46.644
You can."

1519
00:45:46.644 --> 00:45:48.226
And was it just you and Belle?

1520
00:45:48.226 --> 00:45:49.059
That was the crew?

1521
00:45:49.059 --> 00:45:49.927
Was there anybody else?

1522
00:45:49.927 --> 00:45:52.890
Yeah, so, it was me, Belle, and Garrett, my friend.

1523
00:45:52.890 --> 00:45:54.205
So, he was driving the RV.

1524
00:45:54.205 --> 00:45:56.726
He would go every five miles ahead in the beginning.

1525
00:45:56.726 --> 00:45:57.901
So, Belle would be indexed to me,

1526
00:45:57.901 --> 00:46:00.737
literally the top of my eight to 14 hours a day,

1527
00:46:00.737 --> 00:46:04.889
in a support car, driving a RAV4, a crossover,

1528
00:46:04.889 --> 00:46:07.036
where she would be the one doing the direction.

1529
00:46:07.036 --> 00:46:08.179
I'm not good with direction.

1530
00:46:08.179 --> 00:46:09.589
She'll tell me, "Turn when you get to this area."

1531
00:46:09.589 --> 00:46:11.342
And I'm like calling her on my Apple watch,

1532
00:46:11.342 --> 00:46:13.382
"Hey, what street I'm supposed to be turning?"

1533
00:46:13.382 --> 00:46:14.960
But she's next to me for that.

1534
00:46:14.960 --> 00:46:17.970
And like fluids and any snacks or food I need.

1535
00:46:17.970 --> 00:46:19.541
And also for safety too.

1536
00:46:19.541 --> 00:46:23.055
Safety from dogs and some people as well.

1537
00:46:23.055 --> 00:46:24.278
Because there has some people-

1538
00:46:24.278 --> 00:46:27.140
Yeah, I wanna talk about that.

1539
00:46:27.140 --> 00:46:29.255
Also, shooting, editing,

1540
00:46:29.255 --> 00:46:32.332
and taking to the social media the whole time as well.

1541
00:46:32.332 --> 00:46:33.172
Yes. Yeah.

1542
00:46:33.172 --> 00:46:34.005
Doing all of it.

1543
00:46:34.005 --> 00:46:36.704
So, I think if you were to ask me even now

1544
00:46:36.704 --> 00:46:37.986
who had the hardest job, I'd say she did.

1545
00:46:37.986 --> 00:46:41.143
'Cause my energy just had to be solely focused on running

1546
00:46:41.143 --> 00:46:44.317
and just feeling myself, eating and running.

1547
00:46:44.317 --> 00:46:45.482
Hers is like everything.

1548
00:46:45.482 --> 00:46:47.455
She basically held everything together.

1549
00:46:47.455 --> 00:46:48.624
She really did.

1550
00:46:48.624 --> 00:46:52.308
There's an illusion that if your crewing an ultra event,

1551
00:46:52.308 --> 00:46:53.141
that's chill,

1552
00:46:53.141 --> 00:46:55.744
you're just in the car and you're listening to tunes,

1553
00:46:55.744 --> 00:46:58.750
it's full court press, there's so much to do.

1554
00:46:58.750 --> 00:46:59.583
I don't think there's any time, no.

1555
00:46:59.583 --> 00:47:00.487
You have to be thinking ahead.

1556
00:47:00.487 --> 00:47:01.821
You have to be thinking about tomorrow,

1557
00:47:01.821 --> 00:47:02.995
where are we gonna get food?

1558
00:47:02.995 --> 00:47:04.731
Do we have ice?

1559
00:47:04.731 --> 00:47:06.543
Anticipating what your needs are gonna be.

1560
00:47:06.543 --> 00:47:09.726
And also, you're gonna be so exhausted

1561
00:47:09.726 --> 00:47:12.141
that you're not the best arbiter of what you need.

1562
00:47:12.141 --> 00:47:12.974
Exactly.

1563
00:47:12.974 --> 00:47:13.807
Like this guy needs to drink.

1564
00:47:13.807 --> 00:47:14.640
(Hellah laughs)

1565
