1819
00:55:14.736 --> 00:55:15.990
They're in parts of the world.

1820
00:55:15.990 --> 00:55:20.145
And in so many ways, if you're gonna do this,

1821
00:55:20.145 --> 00:55:21.412
you're relying on the kindness of strangers, right?

1822
00:55:21.412 --> 00:55:23.518
Yeah. Yeah.

1823
00:55:23.518 --> 00:55:26.625
As far as I know, you're the first black person

1824
00:55:26.625 --> 00:55:27.582
to do this, right?

1825
00:55:27.582 --> 00:55:28.415
Yeah, to do this solo.

1826
00:55:28.415 --> 00:55:30.978
Yeah, so, I did research to figure out.

1827
00:55:30.978 --> 00:55:34.378
So, back in I think 1928, there are these,

1828
00:55:34.378 --> 00:55:36.525
I think it was three or four runners.

1829
00:55:36.525 --> 00:55:37.358
I'm not sure.

1830
00:55:37.358 --> 00:55:38.335
So, they were running across the country,

1831
00:55:38.335 --> 00:55:40.407
but they were doing a relay.

1832
00:55:40.407 --> 00:55:41.495
So it was-

1833
00:55:41.495 --> 00:55:42.675
And it used to be a race.

1834
00:55:42.675 --> 00:55:43.527
It was like a long time ago.

1835
00:55:43.527 --> 00:55:44.360
Yeah, it was a race, yeah.

1836
00:55:44.360 --> 00:55:45.221
It's literally called Race America or something.

1837
00:55:45.221 --> 00:55:47.201
And there were black dudes in it, yeah, yeah, yeah.

1838
00:55:47.201 --> 00:55:48.229
Yeah, they're actually kicking out

1839
00:55:48.229 --> 00:55:49.533
some of the black runners or color runners.

1840
00:55:49.533 --> 00:55:51.385
They're like, "You're not doing this."

1841
00:55:51.385 --> 00:55:53.935
But they did a thing where it was a relay.

1842
00:55:53.935 --> 00:55:56.336
So, like, let's say me and you did a relay together.

1843
00:55:56.336 --> 00:55:57.360
You do certain amount of distance.

1844
00:55:57.360 --> 00:55:59.876
So, I'm the first solo black person

1845
00:55:59.876 --> 00:56:00.945
in the history of the country

1846
00:56:00.945 --> 00:56:02.828
to run from LA to New York City.

1847
00:56:02.828 --> 00:56:04.097
Did you know that going into this?

1848
00:56:04.097 --> 00:56:05.405
Going into it, I had a conversation with Robbie.

1849
00:56:05.405 --> 00:56:07.295
Robbie actually brought up to me, he said,

1850
00:56:07.295 --> 00:56:09.199
"Hellah, I don't know, I think you might be the first.

1851
00:56:09.199 --> 00:56:10.369
I haven't seen in."

1852
00:56:10.369 --> 00:56:11.637
And Robbie was making sure he was doing his research

1853
00:56:11.637 --> 00:56:14.964
so we don't come and make such statement and it's not true.

1854
00:56:14.964 --> 00:56:18.719
But yeah, I started thinking about it as I was going.

1855
00:56:18.719 --> 00:56:20.793
And that's when I kinda got a little nervous

1856
00:56:20.793 --> 00:56:23.210
with some of the things that's happening in the country.

1857
00:56:23.210 --> 00:56:25.692
So, I asked Robbie, so I called him one day, I said,

1858
00:56:25.692 --> 00:56:27.867
"Hey, what was your biggest fear?"

1859
00:56:27.867 --> 00:56:31.286
So, in my mind, I wasn't even thinking anything else,

1860
00:56:31.286 --> 00:56:33.675
but I was just thinking about being a color person.

1861
00:56:33.675 --> 00:56:36.524
So, he was telling me about the dog situation right away.

1862
00:56:36.524 --> 00:56:37.859
And I brought up the whole

1863
00:56:37.859 --> 00:56:42.069
like should I feel not safe for who I am?

1864
00:56:42.069 --> 00:56:44.678
And then I knew that was something that I was concerned of.

1865
00:56:44.678 --> 00:56:48.088
And you can see why you were concerned about

1866
00:56:48.088 --> 00:56:49.463
when you're in certain parts of the country.

1867
00:56:49.463 --> 00:56:52.043
But overall, I tried not to put my energy into it.

1868
00:56:52.043 --> 00:56:54.047
So, my mentality is, if you put your energy into something,

1869
00:56:54.047 --> 00:56:55.037
that's what's gonna happen.

1870
00:56:55.037 --> 00:56:55.870
You're gonna manifest it.

1871
00:56:55.870 --> 00:56:56.951
So, you're just, yeah, you're coming into

1872
00:56:56.951 --> 00:56:58.350
just positive people.

1873
00:56:58.350 --> 00:57:01.721
And I would say majority of that, 95% of the time,

1874
00:57:01.721 --> 00:57:02.734
that was the case.

1875
00:57:02.734 --> 00:57:03.567
Right.

1876
00:57:03.567 --> 00:57:04.458
You did have a few run-ins though.

1877
00:57:04.458 --> 00:57:06.977
Yeah, I had a few run-ins.

1878
00:57:06.977 --> 00:57:10.130
The first one actually happened in Oklahoma,

1879
00:57:10.130 --> 00:57:12.387
which was really scary for me as that.

1880
00:57:12.387 --> 00:57:14.273
So, when we were in California and Arizona,

1881
00:57:14.273 --> 00:57:16.194
I've had these awesome police officers,

1882
00:57:16.194 --> 00:57:17.880
"Hey, you're the guy on TikTok.

1883
00:57:17.880 --> 00:57:18.871
I saw you on Instagram.

1884
00:57:18.871 --> 00:57:20.202
Can I take a picture with you?"

1885
00:57:20.202 --> 00:57:21.401
I remember this officer,

1886
00:57:21.401 --> 00:57:25.200
I saw him one day outside of Flagstaff, Arizona.

1887
00:57:25.200 --> 00:57:27.954
And then 30 miles later, he saw me the next day he goes,

1888
00:57:27.954 --> 00:57:29.142
"Whoa, you're really making progress."

1889
00:57:29.142 --> 00:57:32.223
And he asked Belle, "Is it okay if I stop Hellah

1890
00:57:32.223 --> 00:57:33.056
to take a picture?

1891
00:57:33.056 --> 00:57:33.889
Is he gonna be mad?"

1892
00:57:33.889 --> 00:57:35.768
And I was like, "No, I'm not gonna be bad."

1893
00:57:35.768 --> 00:57:36.601
So, he came in.

1894
00:57:36.601 --> 00:57:37.464
I was like, "Yes, thank you so much."

1895
00:57:37.464 --> 00:57:39.560
I was always taking pictures with them.

1896
00:57:39.560 --> 00:57:42.530
And one of the officers coming in Oklahoma,

1897
00:57:42.530 --> 00:57:43.867
and I thought it was similar thing.

1898
00:57:43.867 --> 00:57:44.985
Maybe they know what I'm doing.

1899
00:57:44.985 --> 00:57:45.818
So I'm excited.

1900
00:57:45.818 --> 00:57:46.651
I'm running.

1901
00:57:46.651 --> 00:57:47.605
Actually, I was cruising that day.

1902
00:57:47.605 --> 00:57:48.773
I'm like I have my stick.

1903
00:57:48.773 --> 00:57:49.685
I'm like smiling.

1904
00:57:49.685 --> 00:57:51.078
And then I see the officer come out.

1905
00:57:51.078 --> 00:57:53.306
I thought he knew what I was doing.

1906
00:57:53.306 --> 00:57:54.616
But everything kinda got serious immediately.

1907
00:57:54.616 --> 00:57:56.287
I can see it.

1908
00:57:56.287 --> 00:57:58.426
So, he just said, "Hey, sir, I just got a phone call,

1909
00:57:58.426 --> 00:57:59.259
there's a runner on the road.

1910
00:57:59.259 --> 00:58:00.453
What are you doing out here?"

1911
00:58:00.453 --> 00:58:02.296
And with the seriousness of the voice,

1912
00:58:02.296 --> 00:58:05.262
I was like, I don't think he's very happy right now.

1913
00:58:05.262 --> 00:58:06.505
And immediately-

1914
00:58:06.505 --> 00:58:07.425
Is it a busy road?

1915
00:58:07.425 --> 00:58:10.287
I mean, a charitable interpretation would be that

1916
00:58:10.287 --> 00:58:12.058
like why is this guy out here?

1917
00:58:12.058 --> 00:58:13.218
Like it's unsafe or something.

1918
00:58:13.218 --> 00:58:14.370
Yeah, it was in the middle of nowhere.

1919
00:58:14.370 --> 00:58:16.467
Not much traffic to a point where like Belle

1920
00:58:16.467 --> 00:58:18.443
could be next to me for most of the time.

1921
00:58:18.443 --> 00:58:19.715
If anything, she's a little behind or a little ahead.

1922
00:58:19.715 --> 00:58:21.374
It wasn't that busy.

1923
00:58:21.374 --> 00:58:22.236
It was in the middle of nowhere

1924
00:58:22.236 --> 00:58:24.715
with the next town being five miles ahead of me.

1925
00:58:24.715 --> 00:58:26.158
And immediately he said,

1926
00:58:26.158 --> 00:58:27.226
"I got a phone call there's a runner.

1927
00:58:27.226 --> 00:58:28.059
What are you doing out her?

1928
00:58:28.059 --> 00:58:28.892
What's the point of this?"

1929
00:58:28.892 --> 00:58:31.331
And I said, "Oh, I'm actually running across the country."

1930
00:58:31.331 --> 00:58:32.164
He said, "For what?"

1931
00:58:32.164 --> 00:58:34.870
So, what got me scared when he put his hand on his gun.

1932
00:58:34.870 --> 00:58:37.031
And then you know that there's like a clip in the-

1933
00:58:37.031 --> 00:58:37.917
Yeah, yeah, the little box.

1934
00:58:37.917 --> 00:58:40.281
So, I started panicking and I put my stick up

1935
00:58:40.281 --> 00:58:42.192
and said, "Well, this is just a running pole.

1936
00:58:42.192 --> 00:58:43.565
It helps me get up the hills.

1937
00:58:43.565 --> 00:58:45.046
And see, I'm wearing my safety vest.

1938
00:58:45.046 --> 00:58:46.141
I want people to see me.

1939
00:58:46.141 --> 00:58:47.528
I'm doing it for a nonprofit."

1940
00:58:47.528 --> 00:58:48.780
And I just started telling the story.

1941
00:58:48.780 --> 00:58:50.222
And I started waving Belle in.

1942
00:58:50.222 --> 00:58:51.529
And I was scared to wave Belle in early

1943
00:58:51.529 --> 00:58:54.124
because I didn't want him to think that-

1944
00:58:54.124 --> 00:58:55.352
You're calling somebody else.

1945
00:58:55.352 --> 00:58:56.185
I'm getting help,

1946
00:58:56.185 --> 00:58:58.575
and now he has to be protective of himself.

1947
00:58:58.575 --> 00:58:59.408
So, I was scared.

1948
00:58:59.408 --> 00:59:01.603
So, I kinda waited even a little longer to wave her in

1949
00:59:01.603 --> 00:59:03.832
because she was actually thinking later to find out,

1950
00:59:03.832 --> 00:59:05.105
she thought it was just an officer,

1951
00:59:05.105 --> 00:59:06.982
just seeing if I was okay.

1952
00:59:06.982 --> 00:59:08.558
Oh, 'cause it's been the case.

1953
00:59:08.558 --> 00:59:12.596
And then I see these couple far, and these are two couples.

1954
00:59:12.596 --> 00:59:14.016
And I was like, this is weird.

1955
00:59:14.016 --> 00:59:14.915
I think they were waiting for me.

1956
00:59:14.915 --> 00:59:16.285
So, they got impatient with my interaction

1957
00:59:16.285 --> 00:59:17.531
with a police officer.

1958
00:59:17.531 --> 00:59:19.800
At that point he was asking, "Can I see your ID?"

1959
00:59:19.800 --> 00:59:21.816
I said, "Well, my ID is in my RV, five miles ahead.

1960
00:59:21.816 --> 00:59:22.893
I gotta get to that."

1961
00:59:22.893 --> 00:59:24.161
And then he said, "What's your birthday?

1962
00:59:24.161 --> 00:59:25.322
Give me your name."

1963
00:59:25.322 --> 00:59:26.653
And he's just started asking me all these things.

1964
00:59:26.653 --> 00:59:28.459
He was a little annoyed.

1965
00:59:28.459 --> 00:59:31.540
But these couple came in, these white couple came in

1966
00:59:31.540 --> 00:59:32.683
and they're like, "Are you Hellah?

1967
00:59:32.683 --> 00:59:33.769
Our son told us about you.

1968
00:59:33.769 --> 00:59:34.635
We were tracking you down.

1969
00:59:34.635 --> 00:59:35.468
We wanna donate."

1970
00:59:35.468 --> 00:59:36.549
They had money for me.

1971
00:59:36.549 --> 00:59:38.019
They wanted to take pictures.

1972
00:59:38.019 --> 00:59:40.731
Then I see the officer buying into the story.

1973
00:59:40.731 --> 00:59:41.654
I can just see, he's like,

1974
00:59:41.654 --> 00:59:44.090
"Oh, he is actually doing this for real."

1975
00:59:44.090 --> 00:59:45.171
Like he literally can see it.

1976
00:59:45.171 --> 00:59:47.138
And I was like, "Thank God these people came in

1977
00:59:47.138 --> 00:59:48.934
so they can attest to what I'm doing

1978
00:59:48.934 --> 00:59:50.751
'cause they've been tracking and following me."

1979
00:59:50.751 --> 00:59:53.219
And I was waving Belle at that point.

1980
00:59:53.219 --> 00:59:54.052
So, she came in.

1981
00:59:54.052 --> 00:59:55.275
She would come over with the camera all the time

1982
00:59:55.275 --> 00:59:56.437
to get content.

1983
00:59:56.437 --> 01:00:00.468
And the officer asked me then, "Can I also get a picture?"

1984
01:00:00.468 --> 01:00:01.301
Yeah, and I was like-

1985
01:00:01.301 --> 01:00:02.134
At the end of it-

1986
01:00:02.134 --> 01:00:04.359
It just turned into a positive.

1987
01:00:04.359 --> 01:00:05.760
And thank God that happened.

1988
01:00:05.760 --> 01:00:07.328
That was scary.

1989
01:00:07.328 --> 01:00:08.542
It's kinda heavy, man.

1990
01:00:08.542 --> 01:00:12.840
It's heavy that a couple of white people had to come in

1991
01:00:12.840 --> 01:00:15.222
in order for this guy to feel okay about what was happening.

1992
01:00:15.222 --> 01:00:17.680
Yeah, and when he left, it hit me I was shook.

1993
01:00:17.680 --> 01:00:18.947
I couldn't move for like 10 minutes.

1994
01:00:18.947 --> 01:00:20.274
I was in the side of the road.

1995
01:00:20.274 --> 01:00:21.208
I was like, "Wait."

1996
01:00:21.208 --> 01:00:24.404
'Cause I just started thinking, why was he touching his gun?

1997
01:00:24.404 --> 01:00:26.915
And the reason I raised my pole, 'cause I'm thinking,

1998
01:00:26.915 --> 01:00:29.123
I hope no one thinks that's a weapon or a rifle.

1999
01:00:29.123 --> 01:00:29.956
I don't know.

2000
01:00:29.956 --> 01:00:31.565
So, you just started thinking all of these things.

2001
01:00:31.565 --> 01:00:35.106
So, I was shook a little bit and that was tough.

2002
01:00:35.106 --> 01:00:40.023
And also in actually around in California, I had this lady.

2003
01:00:41.169 --> 01:00:43.747
I think the lady was a little cuckoo.

2004
01:00:43.747 --> 01:00:46.572
This lady goes by in a Jeep and she offered me water.

2005
01:00:46.572 --> 01:00:47.920
She said, "Hey, do you want some water to drink?"

2006
01:00:47.920 --> 01:00:49.297
I said, "Oh no, I'm good.

2007
01:00:49.297 --> 01:00:50.130
Thank you.

2008
01:00:50.130 --> 01:00:50.963
That's my support, actually,

2009
01:00:50.963 --> 01:00:51.796
I got my water in there."

2010
01:00:51.796 --> 01:00:54.612
And this lady also is coming up screaming at that car

2011
01:00:54.612 --> 01:00:56.026
for offering you water.

2012
01:00:56.026 --> 01:00:58.049
And then she goes, "What do you think you're doing?"

2013
01:00:58.049 --> 01:00:59.327
I said, "I'm running across the country."

2014
01:00:59.327 --> 01:01:00.645
She said, "For what?"

2015
01:01:00.645 --> 01:01:02.888
I said, "For a nonprofit called Soles4Souls."

2016
01:01:02.888 --> 01:01:05.002
She goes, "Well, that's bullshit.

2017
01:01:05.002 --> 01:01:06.308
You're about to get cut up now."

2018
01:01:06.308 --> 01:01:07.638
I was like, "Wait, is she joking?"

2019
01:01:07.638 --> 01:01:08.654
So, I was like, "Belle, wait, wait."

2020
01:01:08.654 --> 01:01:09.487
Cut off?

2021
01:01:09.487 --> 01:01:10.320
Mm-hmm.

2022
01:01:10.320 --> 01:01:11.532
I was like, "Belle, wait, wait,

2023
01:01:11.532 --> 01:01:13.695
I don't know if she was joking or not, unlock the car."

2024
01:01:13.695 --> 01:01:16.439
And then I'm across the street and she's on the other side.

2025
01:01:16.439 --> 01:01:17.770
And she started charging sprinting.

2026
01:01:17.770 --> 01:01:19.271
And there was a gentleman next to her.

2027
01:01:19.271 --> 01:01:20.116
She was like, "Come."

2028
01:01:20.116 --> 01:01:21.001
I thought it was her boyfriend.

2029
01:01:21.001 --> 01:01:22.756
She's calling her dog to come.

2030
01:01:22.756 --> 01:01:26.425
So, I just sprinted into the car and Belle did a U-turn.

2031
01:01:26.425 --> 01:01:28.475
It was the fastest U-turn I've ever seen her do.

2032
01:01:28.475 --> 01:01:31.002
And we just whipped around and she starts to chase the car.

2033
01:01:31.002 --> 01:01:31.919
And I see her in the...

2034
01:01:31.919 --> 01:01:34.234
I'm turning around, she's chasing the car.

2035
01:01:34.234 --> 01:01:36.161
And she couldn't keep up.

2036
01:01:36.161 --> 01:01:38.656
So, I was kind of, I was thinking in my head,

2037
01:01:38.656 --> 01:01:39.996
there's no way she can catch me right now.

2038
01:01:39.996 --> 01:01:42.165
My leg was good enough to run faster than her,

2039
01:01:42.165 --> 01:01:44.319
but I'm like, if she has a weapon or a gun,

2040
01:01:44.319 --> 01:01:45.386
I can't outrun that.

2041
01:01:45.386 --> 01:01:48.743
So, we call an officer and we waited two hours.

2042
01:01:48.743 --> 01:01:51.392
The nearest officer was like almost an hour away.

2043
01:01:51.392 --> 01:01:53.746
So, we had a two hours Officer Laker.

2044
01:01:53.746 --> 01:01:54.579
That was her last name.

2045
01:01:54.579 --> 01:01:55.412
She was so cool.

2046
01:01:55.412 --> 01:01:56.559
I was, "Oh, Laker, I like that last name."

2047
01:01:56.559 --> 01:01:57.693
She came and escorted us.

2048
01:01:57.693 --> 01:01:59.432
And by the time she got there, they were gone.

2049
01:01:59.432 --> 01:02:02.616
But we just wanted to be safe and to get through that area.

2050
01:02:02.616 --> 01:02:04.747
So, that was in California?

2051
01:02:04.747 --> 01:02:06.317
That was in California in the beginning.

2052
01:02:06.317 --> 01:02:08.244
And a lot of people were warning us to be careful there.

2053
01:02:08.244 --> 01:02:09.526
Yeah.

2054
01:02:09.526 --> 01:02:11.318
And last sad story,

2055
01:02:11.318 --> 01:02:13.803
and I don't like to talk about sad stories so much,

2056
01:02:13.803 --> 01:02:15.420
was Missouri.

2057
01:02:15.420 --> 01:02:17.757
Missouri was one of those places where,

2058
01:02:17.757 --> 01:02:18.996
to begin with, I was already like,

2059
01:02:18.996 --> 01:02:21.553
"I don't like Missouri because of snakes."

2060
01:02:21.553 --> 01:02:22.958
Literally, people were asking me,

2061
01:02:22.958 --> 01:02:23.791
"Have you seen any snakes?"

2062
01:02:23.791 --> 01:02:25.715
I was like, "No, there's snakes nowhere."

2063
01:02:25.715 --> 01:02:28.352
And we get into Missouri, snakes on side of the roads,

2064
01:02:28.352 --> 01:02:30.718
on the grass, everywhere, in front of you.

2065
01:02:30.718 --> 01:02:32.739
You can see road kills, it was really sad to see that.

2066
01:02:32.739 --> 01:02:34.047
So, I'm like, I don't wanna...

2067
01:02:34.047 --> 01:02:36.137
One of them jumped in front of me too,

2068
01:02:36.137 --> 01:02:38.788
and I panicked and screamed and just took off.

2069
01:02:38.788 --> 01:02:40.157
So, that was already in the back of my mind,

2070
01:02:40.157 --> 01:02:42.045
I'm running, I'm like looking at the side of the road,

2071
01:02:42.045 --> 01:02:43.467
I hope there's no snake.

2072
01:02:43.467 --> 01:02:45.857
And I go by Owensville High School

2073
01:02:45.857 --> 01:02:47.128
and school was just getting,

2074
01:02:47.128 --> 01:02:49.049
I was around 2:30, 2:40 PM,

2075
01:02:49.049 --> 01:02:51.737
all a bunch of kids pulling out of the parking lot.

2076
01:02:51.737 --> 01:02:54.368
So, me, whenever I see cars, would always wave.

2077
01:02:54.368 --> 01:02:55.702
Like I say, just give good energy.

2078
01:02:55.702 --> 01:02:58.835
Some cars, they kind of move through so far over,

2079
01:02:58.835 --> 01:02:59.974
even over the white line

2080
01:02:59.974 --> 01:03:00.905
and you feel like you're gonna get hit.

2081
01:03:00.905 --> 01:03:02.407
So, I'm always trying to keep tight

2082
01:03:02.407 --> 01:03:06.096
and also waving at people, I'm here, but also,

2083
01:03:06.096 --> 01:03:08.177
"Hey, hi, how are you doing?"

2084
01:03:08.177 --> 01:03:10.595
And I see these truck poles.

2085
01:03:10.595 --> 01:03:12.686
And then it was a bunch of teenagers,

2086
01:03:12.686 --> 01:03:13.977
bunch of boys in the back of the truck.

2087
01:03:13.977 --> 01:03:17.283
And the pickup truck has a window that rolls down

2088
01:03:17.283 --> 01:03:18.612
in the back windshield.

2089
01:03:18.612 --> 01:03:20.229
So, I saw one of the kids stick their head out

2090
01:03:20.229 --> 01:03:21.470
and call me the N word.

2091
01:03:21.470 --> 01:03:22.303
I was so shocked.

2092
01:03:22.303 --> 01:03:24.227
I was like, "Wait, did this just happen?"

2093
01:03:24.227 --> 01:03:26.920
So, I'm just like, "Come on, what was the point of this?"

2094
01:03:26.920 --> 01:03:29.230
So, Belle across the street thought they were gonna hit me

2095
01:03:29.230 --> 01:03:30.563
'cause sometimes that happens.

2096
01:03:30.563 --> 01:03:32.478
So, she just hunks all the time to warn people.

2097
01:03:32.478 --> 01:03:33.902
She just thought it was one of those.

2098
01:03:33.902 --> 01:03:37.882
And they just ended up kid ducks down and floors it

2099
01:03:37.882 --> 01:03:39.017
and just took off.

2100
01:03:39.017 --> 01:03:40.681
And I'm pretty sure a parent saw it

2101
01:03:40.681 --> 01:03:42.148
because she definitely felt bad.

2102
01:03:42.148 --> 01:03:43.844
She came back around to wave at me

2103
01:03:43.844 --> 01:03:46.867
and basically said, "Hey, I'm sorry that happened."

2104
01:03:46.867 --> 01:03:48.128
So, that happened in Missouri.

2105
01:03:48.128 --> 01:03:49.776
So, that was really...

2106
01:03:49.776 --> 01:03:51.732
And I got flipped off a little bit in Missouri

2107
01:03:51.732 --> 01:03:52.865
prior to that.

2108
01:03:52.865 --> 01:03:54.183
So, that was not a fun day in Missouri.

2109
01:03:54.183 --> 01:03:57.012
Yeah, I'm sorry that that happened.

2110
01:03:57.012 --> 01:03:59.217
But overall people were charitable and awesome.

2111
01:03:59.217 --> 01:04:01.733
Oh, what I realized is there's so many more good people

2112
01:04:01.733 --> 01:04:02.954
in the world than bad.

2113
01:04:02.954 --> 01:04:05.322
And it makes you feel like we have a promising world

2114
01:04:05.322 --> 01:04:08.375
because so many awesome people that don't even know who I am

2115
01:04:08.375 --> 01:04:10.708
were offering me water, they're offering rides

2116
01:04:10.708 --> 01:04:13.044
to a point where like I was denying rides.

2117
01:04:13.044 --> 01:04:14.375
One lady comes to me and say,

2118
01:04:14.375 --> 01:04:15.896
"Well, I won't tell anybody."

2119
01:04:15.896 --> 01:04:17.191
And I was like, "No, that would be cheating."

2120
01:04:17.191 --> 01:04:19.057
Like that's how good people were.

2121
01:04:19.057 --> 01:04:21.547
Bringing Gatorade, they're like, "Well, I saw you.

2122
01:04:21.547 --> 01:04:24.128
I'm like you're not just running a few miles.

2123
01:04:24.128 --> 01:04:25.481
It looks like you're going somewhere far."

2124
01:04:25.481 --> 01:04:27.225
So, they would bring me water.

2125
01:04:27.225 --> 01:04:28.880
And so many good people, so many.

2126
01:04:28.880 --> 01:04:30.111
It's cool.

2127
01:04:30.111 --> 01:04:33.549
Yeah, did you watch Rickey Gates' documentary,

2128
01:04:33.549 --> 01:04:34.707
"Cross Country?"

2129
01:04:34.707 --> 01:04:35.901
No, I don't know if I saw that one.

2130
01:04:35.901 --> 01:04:37.132
You gotta check it out.

2131
01:04:37.132 --> 01:04:37.965
Yeah.

2132
01:04:37.965 --> 01:04:40.819
I mean, because he was doing it self-supported,

2133
01:04:40.819 --> 01:04:41.652
it's just him.

2134
01:04:41.652 --> 01:04:42.842
Oh, he was the one holding the...

2135
01:04:42.842 --> 01:04:43.675
Yes, I saw it.

2136
01:04:43.675 --> 01:04:44.508
Yes, I saw it.

2137
01:04:44.508 --> 01:04:45.341
I did. I did.

2138
01:04:45.341 --> 01:04:48.316
And so much of that movie, it's not about like,

2139
01:04:48.316 --> 01:04:50.558
it's less about the running part

2140
01:04:50.558 --> 01:04:53.234
and it's so much about these encounters that he has

2141
01:04:53.234 --> 01:04:54.489
with all these people along the way.

2142
01:04:54.489 --> 01:04:57.598
And there's like one guy wants to give him money and like...

2143
01:04:57.598 --> 01:04:59.928
And so, and part of the impetus

2144
01:04:59.928 --> 01:05:02.606
for him doing that run when he did it,

2145
01:05:02.606 --> 01:05:06.904
was being this like liberal, progressive guy

2146
01:05:06.904 --> 01:05:08.801
who grew up in Boulder, Colorado.

2147
01:05:08.801 --> 01:05:10.799
Oh yeah, he did a "Transamericana."

2148
01:05:10.799 --> 01:05:11.632
Yeah, exactly.

2149
01:05:11.632 --> 01:05:12.712
Yeah, I saw that.

2150
01:05:12.712 --> 01:05:13.851
I watched that so many times.

2151
01:05:13.851 --> 01:05:14.684
Yeah.

2152
01:05:15.697 --> 01:05:17.981
He wanted to really get a feel

2153
01:05:17.981 --> 01:05:21.746
for what America actually is outside of your Twitter feed

2154
01:05:21.746 --> 01:05:25.759
or what you see in your respective information silo.

2155
01:05:25.759 --> 01:05:30.603
So, I'm curious, outside of these bad experiences

2156
01:05:30.603 --> 01:05:31.436
that you've had,

2157
01:05:31.436 --> 01:05:35.201
like what your take is on the temperature of America.

2158
01:05:35.201 --> 01:05:37.905
Like we're gonna share this on July 4th weekend,

2159
01:05:37.905 --> 01:05:39.339
we're celebrating America.

2160
01:05:39.339 --> 01:05:42.139
America is in a situation right now

2161
01:05:42.139 --> 01:05:45.366
that I would characterize as transitionary at best.

2162
01:05:45.366 --> 01:05:47.569
Like we're very divided.

2163
01:05:47.569 --> 01:05:49.508
And we're struggling with our ability

2164
01:05:49.508 --> 01:05:52.623
to communicate with each other effectively.

2165
01:05:52.623 --> 01:05:56.351
We are, see, there are different worlds out there

2166
01:05:56.351 --> 01:05:58.666
that see things very differently.

2167
01:05:58.666 --> 01:06:01.210
And it's easy when you're staring at a screen

2168
01:06:01.210 --> 01:06:06.210
and kind of taking account of what people are saying online

2169
01:06:06.333 --> 01:06:08.604
to form an opinion of what's actually happening.

2170
01:06:08.604 --> 01:06:10.456
It's a very different thing altogether to be like,

2171
01:06:10.456 --> 01:06:11.570
I'm here on the ground.

2172
01:06:11.570 --> 01:06:12.840
And I went all the way across America.

2173
01:06:12.840 --> 01:06:15.490
And I had conversations with all of these people.

2174
01:06:15.490 --> 01:06:17.880
And this is what my perspective is

2175
01:06:17.880 --> 01:06:19.788
as a result of having had that experience.

2176
01:06:19.788 --> 01:06:20.621
Yeah.

2177
01:06:20.621 --> 01:06:22.621
I think a 1000%, America is much better

2178
01:06:22.621 --> 01:06:24.228
than we see on social media.

2179
01:06:24.228 --> 01:06:25.744
A 100%.

2180
01:06:25.744 --> 01:06:28.144
I really like it's just,

2181
01:06:28.144 --> 01:06:30.460
there've been many days it was so filled with love.

2182
01:06:30.460 --> 01:06:32.337
And you really like to feel love,

2183
01:06:32.337 --> 01:06:35.312
like it's the energy we're literally sitting in the RV

2184
01:06:35.312 --> 01:06:38.224
in awe like, "Wow, this just happened."

2185
01:06:38.224 --> 01:06:39.437
We saw biker go by,

2186
01:06:39.437 --> 01:06:42.503
and then she's asked Garrett in the RV what I was doing.

2187
01:06:42.503 --> 01:06:43.747
She baked vegan cookie.

2188
01:06:43.747 --> 01:06:45.747
Made sure it was vegan 'cause she wants to research on me.

2189
01:06:45.747 --> 01:06:47.812
And came in to even tell us the ingredient too,

2190
01:06:47.812 --> 01:06:49.348
so we can trust her.

2191
01:06:49.348 --> 01:06:50.181
(Rich laughs)

2192
01:06:50.181 --> 01:06:51.146
And came in and found us at a rest stop

2193
01:06:51.146 --> 01:06:53.207
in a Navajo reservation.

2194
01:06:53.207 --> 01:06:55.851
And she was a doctor or a nurse.

2195
01:06:55.851 --> 01:06:59.409
So, people giving, like you said, money,

2196
01:06:59.409 --> 01:07:00.675
literally giving money.

2197
01:07:00.675 --> 01:07:02.066
"Oh, you're doing it for this?

2198
01:07:02.066 --> 01:07:02.899
Here's money.

2199
01:07:02.899 --> 01:07:03.732
Here's cash."

2200
01:07:03.732 --> 01:07:06.336
And it's so much more better.

2201
01:07:06.336 --> 01:07:09.165
It's so much positivity and love and caring

2202
01:07:09.165 --> 01:07:13.953
that I personally felt than I saw from being in New Jersey.

2203
01:07:13.953 --> 01:07:15.263
And being there, you see it for yourself.

2204
01:07:15.263 --> 01:07:17.191
And you can see some of these people don't even have much,

2205
01:07:17.191 --> 01:07:20.069
and they're still trying to make effort

2206
01:07:20.069 --> 01:07:23.235
to make me feel better, to donate, to support.

2207
01:07:23.235 --> 01:07:24.474
Someone was even saying,

2208
01:07:24.474 --> 01:07:26.352
"Hey, you look like you can have some lunch,"

2209
01:07:26.352 --> 01:07:27.970
when I was running across the country.

2210
01:07:27.970 --> 01:07:29.067
I was like, "Nah, I'm good."

2211
01:07:29.067 --> 01:07:29.900
He said, "Just take it."

2212
01:07:29.900 --> 01:07:30.733
And I said, "You know what?

2213
01:07:30.733 --> 01:07:32.853
I'm gonna donate this money exactly to the nonprofit

2214
01:07:32.853 --> 01:07:33.686
I'm running for."

2215
01:07:33.686 --> 01:07:34.519
And he goes, "It's perfect."

2216
01:07:34.519 --> 01:07:35.412
Never seen me.

2217
01:07:35.412 --> 01:07:36.843
Doesn't know who I am, what I do,

2218
01:07:36.843 --> 01:07:38.752
but they just wanted to help.

2219
01:07:38.752 --> 01:07:39.962
And seeing that, that's what I said,

2220
01:07:39.962 --> 01:07:41.484
we have a really promising future.

2221
01:07:41.484 --> 01:07:42.317
That's cool.

2222
01:07:42.317 --> 01:07:43.150
Yeah. Yeah.

2223
01:07:43.150 --> 01:07:43.983
That's encouraging of you.

2224
01:07:43.983 --> 01:07:44.816
It's beautiful.

2225
01:07:44.816 --> 01:07:45.649
It is.

2226
01:07:45.649 --> 01:07:49.535
And then I said 95% of the people, 97 that we've run into,

2227
01:07:49.535 --> 01:07:52.235
it was all nothing but positive energy and love.

2228
01:07:52.235 --> 01:07:55.256
Different background, different race, different gender,

2229
01:07:55.256 --> 01:07:57.365
or whoever they want to be accepted as,

2230
01:07:57.365 --> 01:07:58.619
but you just felt like you were just one.

2231
01:07:58.619 --> 01:08:01.663
And I would ask people questions

2232
01:08:01.663 --> 01:08:02.929
without comes and run with me,

2233
01:08:02.929 --> 01:08:04.368
and I realized we're all the same.

2234
01:08:04.368 --> 01:08:05.370
We all have the same goal.

2235
01:08:05.370 --> 01:08:07.297
We have passionate dreams and goals we wanna accomplish.

2236
01:08:07.297 --> 01:08:08.868
We wanna be able to take care of ourselves, our family,

2237
01:08:08.868 --> 01:08:09.701
and friends.

2238
01:08:09.701 --> 01:08:10.962
And it's just in a different way.

2239
01:08:10.962 --> 01:08:14.117
So, I think we are doing a lot better

2240
01:08:14.117 --> 01:08:15.682
than what we see right now.

2241
01:08:15.682 --> 01:08:16.804
That's to my personal opinion.

2242
01:08:16.804 --> 01:08:17.637
I hope so, man.

2243
01:08:17.637 --> 01:08:18.750
I hope so.

2244
01:08:18.750 --> 01:08:21.123
Well, talk to me about the vegan diet thing.

2245
01:08:21.123 --> 01:08:25.350
It's a whole other like layer to this story.

2246
01:08:25.350 --> 01:08:27.725
So, me going vegan over five years now,

2247
01:08:27.725 --> 01:08:30.350
was five years late February.

2248
01:08:30.350 --> 01:08:34.223
So, Bella went vegetarian the year before.

2249
01:08:34.223 --> 01:08:35.834
We watched "Earthlings" together.

2250
01:08:35.834 --> 01:08:36.976
She's bawling her eyes out.

2251
01:08:36.976 --> 01:08:38.293
She said, "I can never eat animals."

2252
01:08:38.293 --> 01:08:39.637
So, she went vegetarian.

2253
01:08:39.637 --> 01:08:41.209
So, I grew up in West Africa, Mali,

2254
01:08:41.209 --> 01:08:44.521
where I've seen people sacrifice cow, sheep,

2255
01:08:44.521 --> 01:08:47.376
and even was part of holding the legs

2256
01:08:47.376 --> 01:08:48.397
for it to happen as a child.

2257
01:08:48.397 --> 01:08:49.617
They make you do that.

2258
01:08:49.617 --> 01:08:52.424
And you're basically forced into this culture of meat eating

2259
01:08:52.424 --> 01:08:54.707
without even having a choice to.

2260
01:08:54.707 --> 01:08:57.308
And that didn't do anything to me watching "Earthlings."

2261
01:08:57.308 --> 01:08:58.461
And then when I went back to look at it,

2262
01:08:58.461 --> 01:09:00.814
I'm like, "Man, I was sick to watch this

2263
01:09:00.814 --> 01:09:02.064
and not change my last."

2264
01:09:02.064 --> 01:09:03.974
I was even sad watching it.

2265
01:09:03.974 --> 01:09:05.909
But fast forward to a year later,

2266
01:09:05.909 --> 01:09:07.666
she wanted me to watch this documentary

2267
01:09:07.666 --> 01:09:09.064
called "Forks Over Knives."

2268
01:09:09.064 --> 01:09:10.747
So, I said, "Let's just do it."

2269
01:09:10.747 --> 01:09:11.746
I gotta start listening to her,

2270
01:09:11.746 --> 01:09:13.462
because every time I listened to do something,

2271
01:09:13.462 --> 01:09:14.866
it ends up being amazing.

2272
01:09:14.866 --> 01:09:16.199
And we watch it.

2273
01:09:17.391 --> 01:09:18.335
(laughs) Why is that?

2274
01:09:18.335 --> 01:09:19.168
I don't know.

2275
01:09:19.168 --> 01:09:20.001
She's just amazing.

2276
01:09:20.001 --> 01:09:20.834
She's incredible.

2277
01:09:20.834 --> 01:09:22.441
So, 20 minutes into "Forks Over Knives,"

2278
01:09:22.441 --> 01:09:23.873
I remember this vividly.

2279
01:09:23.873 --> 01:09:25.156
I looked at her with my mouth dropped.

2280
01:09:25.156 --> 01:09:26.121
She goes, "Are you okay?"

2281
01:09:26.121 --> 01:09:27.746
I said, "I don't think I'm okay

2282
01:09:27.746 --> 01:09:29.025
because I don't think I could ever eat meat

2283
01:09:29.025 --> 01:09:30.231
for the rest of my life, but I'm scared.

2284
01:09:30.231 --> 01:09:31.450
I don't know what to eat."

2285
01:09:31.450 --> 01:09:32.562
And she said, "Don't worry about it.

2286
01:09:32.562 --> 01:09:33.395
We'll figure it out."

2287
01:09:33.395 --> 01:09:35.550
So, we went vegan together, cold turkey.

2288
01:09:35.550 --> 01:09:38.360
So, I made a decision right then, I'm never eating animals,

2289
01:09:38.360 --> 01:09:40.023
seeing what it does to people,

2290
01:09:40.023 --> 01:09:41.614
seeing professional athlete being on plat-based

2291
01:09:41.614 --> 01:09:44.284
and doing their stuff at the elite level

2292
01:09:44.284 --> 01:09:45.154
and I'm an amateur.

2293
01:09:45.154 --> 01:09:46.470
If they can do at an elite level,

2294
01:09:46.470 --> 01:09:50.152
why can't I survive being who I am and not eat animal.

2295
01:09:50.152 --> 01:09:52.761
So, I became vegan for selfish reason.

2296
01:09:52.761 --> 01:09:54.717
And now it's more than that.

2297
01:09:54.717 --> 01:09:56.110
It's more ethical for me too as well.

2298
01:09:56.110 --> 01:09:58.649
So, I'm glad it took that

2299
01:09:58.649 --> 01:10:00.718
for me to realize what's happening in the world,

2300
01:10:00.718 --> 01:10:01.859
even our climate or whatever.

2301
01:10:01.859 --> 01:10:03.796
But the only thing I regret about going vegan

2302
01:10:03.796 --> 01:10:06.643
and being plant-based is I didn't do it soon enough.

2303
01:10:06.643 --> 01:10:07.776
That's the only thing.

2304
01:10:07.776 --> 01:10:08.609
Yeah, that's interesting.

2305
01:10:08.609 --> 01:10:12.070
So, you were doing it before the run streak-

2306
01:10:12.070 --> 01:10:13.002
Yeah, the run streak, yeah.

2307
01:10:13.002 --> 01:10:15.346
When you were still in the professional soccer world.

2308
01:10:15.346 --> 01:10:17.727
Yeah, actually, right when I turned vegan,

2309
01:10:17.727 --> 01:10:19.851
I want to play in Oklahoma City for the Oklahoma City Energy

2310
01:10:19.851 --> 01:10:22.814
there in the USL, the lower division,

2311
01:10:22.814 --> 01:10:25.122
just the division below MLS.

2312
01:10:25.122 --> 01:10:26.023
And I got there.

2313
01:10:26.023 --> 01:10:27.281
I used to get kicked out of practice.

2314
01:10:27.281 --> 01:10:28.899
I'm not kidding you.

2315
01:10:28.899 --> 01:10:29.732
Wow.

2316
01:10:29.732 --> 01:10:32.491
I had this energy that my body just started feeling

2317
01:10:32.491 --> 01:10:33.830
and I just couldn't explain it.

2318
01:10:33.830 --> 01:10:35.716
And my teammate would look at me, "Are you crazy, Hellah?

2319
01:10:35.716 --> 01:10:37.320
What's going on with you?"

2320
01:10:37.320 --> 01:10:40.751
I remember one game at a locker room.

2321
01:10:40.751 --> 01:10:43.852
Half time, one of our teammates goes,

2322
01:10:43.852 --> 01:10:46.006
"If you come in this locker room and you don't feel like

2323
01:10:46.006 --> 01:10:47.036
you haven't left everything on the field,

2324
01:10:47.036 --> 01:10:48.840
you're not exhausted, that means you didn't play."

2325
01:10:48.840 --> 01:10:50.117
So, I humbly raised my hand.

2326
01:10:50.117 --> 01:10:51.827
I said, "I disagree with that

2327
01:10:51.827 --> 01:10:54.475
because every game I've been giving all my all,

2328
01:10:54.475 --> 01:10:55.739
but I still feel like I can play a second game."

2329
01:10:55.739 --> 01:10:58.171
That's how much energy my body just felt.

2330
01:10:58.171 --> 01:10:59.457
So, just because I don't feel tired

2331
01:10:59.457 --> 01:11:02.112
doesn't mean I didn't leave it all out on the field.

2332
01:11:02.112 --> 01:11:02.945
And I used to,

2333
01:11:02.945 --> 01:11:04.204
that energy, it was just people.

2334
01:11:04.204 --> 01:11:07.657
And I started convincing my teammates to go plant-based.

2335
01:11:07.657 --> 01:11:08.490
Then I had to do this.

2336
01:11:08.490 --> 01:11:09.343
I just don't eat animal.

2337
01:11:09.343 --> 01:11:11.397
My recovery time is quicker and things like that.

2338
01:11:11.397 --> 01:11:12.356
And I can feel it.

2339
01:11:12.356 --> 01:11:14.874
How long before you had that experience

2340
01:11:14.874 --> 01:11:16.600
after making the switch?

2341
01:11:16.600 --> 01:11:18.907
I switched a month later.

2342
01:11:18.907 --> 01:11:20.309
I went to Oklahoma to play.

2343
01:11:20.309 --> 01:11:21.559
It was like about a month later.

2344
01:11:21.559 --> 01:11:22.392
Wow.

2345
01:11:22.392 --> 01:11:23.225
Yeah, literally.

2346
01:11:23.225 --> 01:11:24.590
Switched in February or March.

2347
01:11:24.590 --> 01:11:26.373
1st of April I was in Oklahoma.

2348
01:11:26.373 --> 01:11:28.070
So, recovery times are better

2349
01:11:28.070 --> 01:11:29.711
without running out of energy.

2350
01:11:29.711 --> 01:11:31.939
Not like petering out in fourth quarter

2351
01:11:31.939 --> 01:11:33.385
or late second half or whatever.

2352
01:11:33.385 --> 01:11:35.226
As being young, we would be up to 2:00, 3:00

2353
01:11:35.226 --> 01:11:37.271
in the morning, we wake up, everybody's exhausted,

2354
01:11:37.271 --> 01:11:38.762
like, "I don't know how we're gonna survive practice."

2355
01:11:38.762 --> 01:11:40.768
I'm like, "I feel like I got enough rest."

2356
01:11:40.768 --> 01:11:42.654
And then when I started seeing them like,

2357
01:11:42.654 --> 01:11:44.131
"Wow, I think it's my diet.

2358
01:11:44.131 --> 01:11:45.405
It has to be."

2359
01:11:45.405 --> 01:11:46.778
'Cause I was a big chicken person.

2360
01:11:46.778 --> 01:11:48.857
In fact, I'd have leftover chicken from night

2361
01:11:48.857 --> 01:11:51.019
and eat it as breakfast that morning,

2362
01:11:51.019 --> 01:11:53.124
like 8:00, 9:00 in the morning, which is really-

2363
01:11:53.124 --> 01:11:54.485
They wanna kick you out of practice?

2364
01:11:54.485 --> 01:11:57.815
Yeah, my coach would be like, Hey, Hellah,

2365
01:11:57.815 --> 01:11:58.737
you're done for the day."

2366
01:11:58.737 --> 01:12:00.929
'Cause the second team that doesn't play a lot,

2367
01:12:00.929 --> 01:12:02.216
they practiced longer to get more fitness

2368
01:12:02.216 --> 01:12:03.912
and gamma underneath them.

2369
01:12:03.912 --> 01:12:05.854
Oh, 'cause you had to play, he didn't wanna burn you out.

2370
01:12:05.854 --> 01:12:07.747
Yeah, that's why I got kicked out of practice.

2371
01:12:07.747 --> 01:12:10.726
So, I would go join them to do extra practices.

2372
01:12:10.726 --> 01:12:11.810
And my coach would,

2373
01:12:11.810 --> 01:12:14.091
or like easy day where we don't play much

2374
01:12:14.091 --> 01:12:16.280
and I wanna stay long, he's like, "Hellah, you're done.

2375
01:12:16.280 --> 01:12:17.360
You have a game in two days."

2376
01:12:17.360 --> 01:12:19.277
And I wanna stay, but I always get kicked out,

2377
01:12:19.277 --> 01:12:21.338
'cause I had that energy with me

2378
01:12:21.338 --> 01:12:23.361
I think because of plant-based.

2379
01:12:23.361 --> 01:12:26.214
Do you know this soccer agent called Daren Flitcroft?

2380
01:12:26.214 --> 01:12:27.321
Heard of him. Heard of him.

2381
01:12:27.321 --> 01:12:28.154
Yeah, he's a friend of mine.

2382
01:12:28.154 --> 01:12:28.987
Oh, really?

2383
01:12:28.987 --> 01:12:29.820
But he's super plant-based.

2384
01:12:29.820 --> 01:12:31.244
Oh, wow, that's cool.

2385
01:12:31.244 --> 01:12:34.298
And he's a big mucky muck in that soccer agenting world

2386
01:12:34.298 --> 01:12:35.243
or whatever.

2387
01:12:35.243 --> 01:12:37.158
But he's like gung-ho plant-based.

2388
01:12:37.158 --> 01:12:37.991
Yeah.

2389
01:12:37.991 --> 01:12:39.231
And a fun fact actually,

2390
01:12:39.231 --> 01:12:44.231
so my neighbor, Samuel and his girlfriend, Roberta Greiner,

2391
01:12:44.773 --> 01:12:47.815
who was actually was ranked in Doha for- four marathon

2392
01:12:47.815 --> 01:12:49.465
as he was running six in the world.

2393
01:12:49.465 --> 01:12:50.298
Wow.

2394
01:12:50.298 --> 01:12:51.131
So, they saw,

2395
01:12:51.131 --> 01:12:54.360
I kinda started telling them about the whole vegan thing.

2396
01:12:54.360 --> 01:12:56.778
So, that surprised me with your book "Plantpower."

2397
01:12:56.778 --> 01:12:57.611
Oh cool.

2398
01:12:57.611 --> 01:12:59.911
Yeah, so, I was literally consuming your book.

2399
01:12:59.911 --> 01:13:00.744
Oh, good.

2400
01:13:00.744 --> 01:13:01.577
Before the transcontinental.

2401
01:13:01.577 --> 01:13:02.689
Oh, that makes me feel good. (laughs)

2402
01:13:02.689 --> 01:13:03.756
Yeah, I have your book at home.

2403
01:13:03.756 --> 01:13:04.914
So, they'll give it to me as a gift.

2404
01:13:04.914 --> 01:13:06.871
I don't have it list for my birthday last November,

2405
01:13:06.871 --> 01:13:09.088
but it was, they say here's a book.

2406
01:13:09.088 --> 01:13:10.114
I was like, "Oh, Rich Rolls?"

2407
01:13:10.114 --> 01:13:11.797
I didn't know you had that book.

2408
01:13:11.797 --> 01:13:14.885
So, superfood, so there was a chapter with the superfoods.

2409
01:13:14.885 --> 01:13:16.181
So, I was just saying, "Okay, Hellah,

2410
01:13:16.181 --> 01:13:18.086
you're tending to run across the country now.

2411
01:13:18.086 --> 01:13:19.310
Yes, you're vegan.

2412
01:13:19.310 --> 01:13:20.595
So, now let's add more superfoods

2413
01:13:20.595 --> 01:13:22.544
because now you're doing something

2414
01:13:22.544 --> 01:13:24.623
that your body is not used to.

2415
01:13:24.623 --> 01:13:25.740
So, I need the food.

2416
01:13:25.740 --> 01:13:28.137
So, again, thank you for having that out there-

2417
01:13:28.137 --> 01:13:28.970
You're very welcome.

2418
01:13:28.970 --> 01:13:29.960
For all the plant-based people out there.

2419
01:13:29.960 --> 01:13:33.188
No, I'm glad that I was able to contribute some small

2420
01:13:33.188 --> 01:13:35.131
into this from afar.

2421
01:13:35.131 --> 01:13:39.317
So, what did the daily nutritional situation look like

2422
01:13:39.317 --> 01:13:41.097
when you were running across the country?

2423
01:13:41.097 --> 01:13:46.097
So, my, I had sponsors, Vivo Life, which is a 100% vegan

2424
01:13:46.690 --> 01:13:47.997
their mantra is, "For the living."

2425
01:13:47.997 --> 01:13:48.871
Like out of the UK.

2426
01:13:48.871 --> 01:13:49.830
Yeah, UK, yeah.

2427
01:13:49.830 --> 01:13:50.663
For the living.

2428
01:13:50.663 --> 01:13:51.779
And the reason I wanted to work with them

2429
01:13:51.779 --> 01:13:55.418
because they plant trees every time someone buys something.

2430
01:13:55.418 --> 01:13:59.014
So, over 250,000 trees in a year from their sales.

2431
01:13:59.014 --> 01:14:00.989
So, they kind of asked me,

2432
01:14:00.989 --> 01:14:02.522
"Hellah, can you write out all the stuff you eat?"

2433
01:14:02.522 --> 01:14:04.440
So, there was a nutritionist there.

2434
01:14:04.440 --> 01:14:05.273
So, I kinda did.

2435
01:14:05.273 --> 01:14:06.380
And they kinda put that in together.

2436
01:14:06.380 --> 01:14:07.474
And I told them what I wanna eat.

2437
01:14:07.474 --> 01:14:09.720
Some of the stuff I looked at in your book,

2438
01:14:09.720 --> 01:14:10.714
this is what I wanna get myself.

2439
01:14:10.714 --> 01:14:13.255
So, we were doing like a practice feeling.

2440
01:14:13.255 --> 01:14:15.187
Like stuffing myself, being uncomfortable,

2441
01:14:15.187 --> 01:14:18.692
running with food in my hand to eat and train that.

2442
01:14:18.692 --> 01:14:19.958
And so, my biggest thing was bagels.

2443
01:14:19.958 --> 01:14:21.125
I love bagels.

2444
01:14:21.967 --> 01:14:23.232
But I got sick of bagels.

2445
01:14:23.232 --> 01:14:24.491
So, but I was eating a lot of the rice whole.

2446
01:14:24.491 --> 01:14:25.728
It's hard to eat.

2447
01:14:25.728 --> 01:14:29.317
Well, you can pour water on them and they go down easier.

2448
01:14:29.317 --> 01:14:30.909
But while you're running, you can try bagel.

2449
01:14:30.909 --> 01:14:31.844
I don't know about that.

2450
01:14:31.844 --> 01:14:32.677
Yeah, exactly.

2451
01:14:32.677 --> 01:14:34.806
So, I was leading a lot of the rice bowls,

2452
01:14:34.806 --> 01:14:37.787
the fresh veggies, avocado.

2453
01:14:37.787 --> 01:14:39.143
Belle was really creative with the food

2454
01:14:39.143 --> 01:14:40.964
to make me more interested in it

2455
01:14:40.964 --> 01:14:42.449
'cause my appetite would change.

2456
01:14:42.449 --> 01:14:44.708
I would be obsessed with certain food.

2457
01:14:44.708 --> 01:14:47.176
Within few days, I can't even look at it or smell it.

2458
01:14:47.176 --> 01:14:51.216
So, we were eating a lot of whole foods and a lot of green,

2459
01:14:51.216 --> 01:14:52.217
everything you can imagine,

2460
01:14:52.217 --> 01:14:54.763
and hydrating with electrolyte mostly then water.

2461
01:14:54.763 --> 01:14:55.596
Yeah.

2462
01:14:55.596 --> 01:14:57.339
Did you have a Vitamix on the RV?

2463
01:14:57.339 --> 01:14:59.649
We had a blender, but not a Vitamix

2464
01:14:59.649 --> 01:15:01.782
because we were scared is it gonna use all the power.

2465
01:15:01.782 --> 01:15:03.526
Yeah, because it requires a little bit more power.

2466
01:15:03.526 --> 01:15:04.630
Yeah, a little bit more power, yeah.

2467
01:15:04.630 --> 01:15:06.534
But then you use a normal blender,

2468
01:15:06.534 --> 01:15:07.430
it's not the same thing.

2469
01:15:07.430 --> 01:15:08.345
Yeah, it's not the same thing.

2470
01:15:08.345 --> 01:15:09.477
Yeah.

2471
01:15:09.477 --> 01:15:11.914
How much of the intake was liquid

2472
01:15:11.914 --> 01:15:13.791
versus like solid foods?

2473
01:15:13.791 --> 01:15:15.107
Actually, I'm actually surprised,

2474
01:15:15.107 --> 01:15:17.114
I was eating more solid and liquid.

2475
01:15:17.114 --> 01:15:19.244
So, my biggest liquid would be at nighttime.

2476
01:15:19.244 --> 01:15:21.410
So, we would do a Ben &amp; Jerry's vegan ice cream,

2477
01:15:21.410 --> 01:15:23.851
where she would pour that with oat milk.

2478
01:15:23.851 --> 01:15:24.861
A 1000 calorie.

2479
01:15:24.861 --> 01:15:26.165
The Ben &amp; Jerry's was 990 calories.

2480
01:15:26.165 --> 01:15:28.844
And with oat milk, I had to get over 1000 calories.

2481
01:15:28.844 --> 01:15:30.464
Blended, I eat my dinner and I just chugged that.

2482
01:15:30.464 --> 01:15:31.658
(Rich laughs)

2483
01:15:31.658 --> 01:15:32.491
So, I was getting-

2484
01:15:32.491 --> 01:15:33.719
The Ben &amp; Jerry's vegan ice cream.

2485
01:15:33.719 --> 01:15:37.311
Yeah, that was the best for me, for liquid.

2486
01:15:37.311 --> 01:15:39.140
And then now we started having the electrolytes

2487
01:15:39.140 --> 01:15:40.965
that has calories in it to drink that,

2488
01:15:40.965 --> 01:15:43.395
to making sure that when I'm drinking electrolytes,

2489
01:15:43.395 --> 01:15:44.689
I'm not just drinking for the electrolytes,

2490
01:15:44.689 --> 01:15:47.023
but I'm getting some calories off of it as well.

2491
01:15:47.023 --> 01:15:47.856
So...

2492
01:15:47.856 --> 01:15:49.842
And what kind of heart rate were you maintaining?

2493
01:15:49.842 --> 01:15:50.675
I was trying.

2494
01:15:50.675 --> 01:15:53.421
My goal was keep it below 140.

2495
01:15:53.421 --> 01:15:54.254
Do that.

2496
01:15:54.254 --> 01:15:55.087
So, people would come-

2497
01:15:55.087 --> 01:15:55.920
Low zone two.

2498
01:15:55.920 --> 01:15:56.753
Yeah.

2499
01:15:56.753 --> 01:15:57.586
I mean, I don't know what your thresholds are.

2500
01:15:57.586 --> 01:15:59.029
Yeah, people would come run with me

2501
01:15:59.029 --> 01:16:01.037
and then they kind of start pulling away,

2502
01:16:01.037 --> 01:16:03.219
and start to be like, "Don't do it, Hellah.

2503
01:16:03.219 --> 01:16:05.521
Because you have to not just survive today,

2504
01:16:05.521 --> 01:16:07.020
you have tomorrow and the next and the next day to see it.

2505
01:16:07.020 --> 01:16:07.928
You're playing the long game.

2506
01:16:07.928 --> 01:16:09.691
Yeah, they're just here for the day.

2507
01:16:09.691 --> 01:16:10.777
'Cause then they don't do it on purpose.

2508
01:16:10.777 --> 01:16:13.822
They just like kinda, you just drift away somewhere

2509
01:16:13.822 --> 01:16:16.321
when it's a group of people and I just stayed behind.

2510
01:16:16.321 --> 01:16:17.458
I said, "Yeah, you guys can keep going.

2511
01:16:17.458 --> 01:16:19.877
I'll see you when I see you."

2512
01:16:19.877 --> 01:16:21.146
How was the sleep?

2513
01:16:21.146 --> 01:16:22.306
I couldn't sleep.

2514
01:16:22.306 --> 01:16:23.139
That was the problem.

2515
01:16:23.139 --> 01:16:24.905
I'd always wake up tossing and turning at night.

2516
01:16:24.905 --> 01:16:26.223
It wasn't because the RV bed was uncomfortable.

2517
01:16:26.223 --> 01:16:28.069
I thought that was the most comfortable bed,

2518
01:16:28.069 --> 01:16:29.917
but it's just that I just can't sleep.

2519
01:16:29.917 --> 01:16:31.725
I wake up at 2:00 in the morning,

2520
01:16:31.725 --> 01:16:33.489
up for two hours and I'd fall asleep.

2521
01:16:33.489 --> 01:16:35.344
The alarm is ringing 6:30.

2522
01:16:35.344 --> 01:16:36.177
You gotta get up.

2523
01:16:36.177 --> 01:16:37.010
So, I think on average,

2524
01:16:37.010 --> 01:16:39.062
I got less than five hours of sleep the whole time

2525
01:16:39.062 --> 01:16:39.953
for the 84 days.

2526
01:16:39.953 --> 01:16:41.139
Were you're wearing like a WHOOP

2527
01:16:41.139 --> 01:16:43.749
or any kinda tracker that could give you some data on sleep?

2528
01:16:43.749 --> 01:16:46.455
I just used my Garmin.

2529
01:16:46.455 --> 01:16:47.755
And I used to wear a WHOOP,

2530
01:16:47.755 --> 01:16:50.323
but I didn't bring the WHOOP with me.

2531
01:16:50.323 --> 01:16:52.973
I used to have that, but I just used the Garmin

2532
01:16:52.973 --> 01:16:54.478
and just went off of.

2533
01:16:54.478 --> 01:16:56.587
'Cause to me, even when I was using WHOOP,

2534
01:16:56.587 --> 01:16:57.882
it would tell me to take a day off

2535
01:16:57.882 --> 01:16:59.598
and there's no day off for me.

2536
01:16:59.598 --> 01:17:04.296
(laughs) Your strain score is 20-plus today.

2537
01:17:04.296 --> 01:17:05.564
Time to time to give it a rest.

2538
01:17:05.564 --> 01:17:06.479
Yeah, exactly.

2539
01:17:06.479 --> 01:17:08.189
That's not now what you wanna hear.

2540
01:17:08.189 --> 01:17:09.805
You've got 47 miles ahead of you.

2541
01:17:09.805 --> 01:17:10.638
Exactly.

2542
01:17:10.638 --> 01:17:11.471
I love my Garmin.

2543
01:17:11.471 --> 01:17:13.729
I think is the best precious I've done.

2544
01:17:13.729 --> 01:17:15.018
It does everything that I need to do.

2545
01:17:15.018 --> 01:17:16.639
It also tells me all of these numbers

2546
01:17:16.639 --> 01:17:17.986
that I needed to know for my body.

2547
01:17:17.986 --> 01:17:20.076
But every time I started started run,

2548
01:17:20.076 --> 01:17:22.549
it says, "Suggestion to rest."

2549
01:17:22.549 --> 01:17:23.394
Take a day off. (laughs)

2550
01:17:23.394 --> 01:17:25.427
Yeah, and it will say to me,

2551
01:17:25.427 --> 01:17:27.561
"Your fitness goal, take 12 days off."

2552
01:17:27.561 --> 01:17:29.522
I'm like, "Wait, I can't do this.

2553
01:17:29.522 --> 01:17:30.659
There's no day off for this.

2554
01:17:30.659 --> 01:17:31.886
You gotta get up and go."

2555
01:17:31.886 --> 01:17:33.545
And so, the technology will tell you,

2556
01:17:33.545 --> 01:17:34.875
"Hey, you're doing too much training,"

2557
01:17:34.875 --> 01:17:37.201
but you just gotta keep pushing through.

2558
01:17:37.201 --> 01:17:38.077
I was talking to...

2559
01:17:38.077 --> 01:17:40.056
Did you follow the Iron Cowboy dude?

2560
01:17:40.056 --> 01:17:40.925
Oh, he's amazing.

2561
01:17:40.925 --> 01:17:42.189
James, I talked to him.

2562
01:17:42.189 --> 01:17:43.022
Did you talk to him?

2563
01:17:43.022 --> 01:17:43.910
Yeah, I talked to James.

2564
01:17:43.910 --> 01:17:45.268
He actually DMed me too.

2565
01:17:45.268 --> 01:17:47.950
And then he's like he congratulated me.

2566
01:17:47.950 --> 01:17:49.189
I'm like, "Wait, look, do you know what you just did?"

2567
01:17:49.189 --> 01:17:50.052
Oh, it's cool.

2568
01:17:50.052 --> 01:17:51.314
Yeah. I love.

2569
01:17:51.314 --> 01:17:53.061
And I was trying to see if I can,

2570
01:17:53.061 --> 01:17:54.997
we were thinking, oh, is he gonna be in my path?

2571
01:17:54.997 --> 01:17:56.412
So, I joined him.

2572
01:17:56.412 --> 01:17:58.635
And then we realized he's in Utah.

2573
01:17:58.635 --> 01:17:59.475
So, that was out of the question.

2574
01:17:59.475 --> 01:18:02.978
So, when I got back, I was trying to see if I can get to him

2575
01:18:02.978 --> 01:18:05.505
and do some miles with him, but I didn't get the chance.

2576
01:18:05.505 --> 01:18:06.638
You wouldn't be able to meet him.

2577
01:18:06.638 --> 01:18:07.708
Maybe I wanna meet him one day.

2578
01:18:07.708 --> 01:18:09.076
Yeah, I can look that up for you.

2579
01:18:09.076 --> 01:18:10.490
I showed up on day 91.

2580
01:18:10.490 --> 01:18:11.507
I saw that.

2581
01:18:11.507 --> 01:18:12.358
I was so jealous.

2582
01:18:12.358 --> 01:18:13.369
I'm like, "Oh, Rich is there with... "

2583
01:18:13.369 --> 01:18:14.202
It was pretty fun.

2584
01:18:14.202 --> 01:18:15.035
Yeah.

2585
01:18:15.035 --> 01:18:16.003
But he was telling me,

2586
01:18:16.003 --> 01:18:17.704
'cause I asked him about his sleep as well.

2587
01:18:17.704 --> 01:18:20.557
And he said that his sleep was terrible.

2588
01:18:20.557 --> 01:18:22.353
It was terrible during this thing.

2589
01:18:22.353 --> 01:18:26.510
He would have night sweats and night terrors.

2590
01:18:26.510 --> 01:18:29.102
He would sleepwalk like he was all jacked up.

2591
01:18:29.102 --> 01:18:33.038
Like he's like, "I never have nightmares or night terrors."

2592
01:18:33.038 --> 01:18:35.033
But it was like a really weird thing.

2593
01:18:35.033 --> 01:18:38.494
So, even though he would be flat on his back,

2594
01:18:38.494 --> 01:18:40.175
he wasn't really actually sleeping

2595
01:18:40.175 --> 01:18:41.957
because his body was so traumatized

2596
01:18:41.957 --> 01:18:43.053
by what he was putting it through.

2597
01:18:43.053 --> 01:18:43.968
In shock for me too.

2598
01:18:43.968 --> 01:18:45.666
I can't even imagine for him,

2599
01:18:45.666 --> 01:18:49.514
'cause he's just an incredible doing all that,

2600
01:18:49.514 --> 01:18:50.692
getting up and repeating.

2601
01:18:50.692 --> 01:18:52.665
And you know what's fascinating to me about what he did?

2602
01:18:52.665 --> 01:18:55.299
For me, what made it very fun to,

2603
01:18:55.299 --> 01:18:56.462
you know you're making progress.

2604
01:18:56.462 --> 01:18:57.680
I'm going east, no matter what.

2605
01:18:57.680 --> 01:18:58.747
Every mile is counting.

2606
01:18:58.747 --> 01:19:00.009
Except some days when you're climbing up,

2607
01:19:00.009 --> 01:19:02.065
you're like, "Ah, I'm not even going east yet."

2608
01:19:02.065 --> 01:19:04.054
But he has to do his in the same area over and over.

2609
01:19:04.054 --> 01:19:04.887
Right.

2610
01:19:04.887 --> 01:19:07.222
It would be like you waking up in your house in New Jersey

2611
01:19:07.222 --> 01:19:09.543
and doing a 40 to 50-mile loop every day, the same way.

2612
01:19:09.543 --> 01:19:12.612
Yeah, I think huge props to him mentally,

2613
01:19:12.612 --> 01:19:13.926
just to be well to sustain that.

2614
01:19:13.926 --> 01:19:17.124
Because you're in the same area, it's not changing.

2615
01:19:17.124 --> 01:19:18.068
It can get boring.

2616
01:19:18.068 --> 01:19:18.990
It could be whatever.

2617
01:19:18.990 --> 01:19:19.823
And he still did it.

2618
01:19:19.823 --> 01:19:22.989
And I wanted what it was the next day.

2619
01:19:22.989 --> 01:19:25.036
I saw and I'm like, "What's happening?"

2620
01:19:25.036 --> 01:19:26.726
Because he just wanted to blow people's minds.

2621
01:19:26.726 --> 01:19:27.559
Yeah, he did.

2622
01:19:27.559 --> 01:19:29.059
And the point is made,

2623
01:19:29.059 --> 01:19:31.211
that even when you meet your goal,

2624
01:19:31.211 --> 01:19:33.805
like even when you do the thing that you

2625
01:19:33.805 --> 01:19:36.300
and probably nobody else thought was possible,

2626
01:19:36.300 --> 01:19:37.457
you still have more in you.

2627
01:19:37.457 --> 01:19:38.290
Exactly.

2628
01:19:38.290 --> 01:19:39.462
There's always one more.

2629
01:19:39.462 --> 01:19:40.295
There's always one more.

2630
01:19:40.295 --> 01:19:41.914
And where this transcontinental,

2631
01:19:41.914 --> 01:19:43.975
what I really learned is where I knew this,

2632
01:19:43.975 --> 01:19:46.624
but like we're really much stronger than we think we are.

2633
01:19:46.624 --> 01:19:48.466
When you're put in an uncomfortable situation,

2634
01:19:48.466 --> 01:19:50.097
you'll find a way out if you have no option.

2635
01:19:50.097 --> 01:19:53.195
So, my mentality, get comfortable with the uncomfortable.

2636
01:19:53.195 --> 01:19:54.880
And this is what really taught me.

2637
01:19:54.880 --> 01:19:56.763
So, if anyone who's struggling with anything right now,

2638
01:19:56.763 --> 01:19:57.643
just stick to it,

2639
01:19:57.643 --> 01:19:58.882
because eventually there'll be a turning point.

2640
01:19:58.882 --> 01:20:00.086
You just have to fight through.

2641
01:20:00.086 --> 01:20:01.039
Fight the day.

2642
01:20:01.039 --> 01:20:02.285
And there's been many days

2643
01:20:02.285 --> 01:20:03.858
where I'm just like, "Survive today."

2644
01:20:03.858 --> 01:20:05.223
I don't care about tomorrow, what happened yesterday,

2645
01:20:05.223 --> 01:20:06.748
just survive today.

2646
01:20:06.748 --> 01:20:07.859
So, it comes down to that.

2647
01:20:07.859 --> 01:20:09.429
So, when you would have those days,

2648
01:20:09.429 --> 01:20:10.819
when you would wake up and you're like,

2649
01:20:10.819 --> 01:20:12.744
"There's no way I can do it,"

2650
01:20:12.744 --> 01:20:16.472
walk me through the mantra or how you get yourself

2651
01:20:16.472 --> 01:20:18.959
into the mindset to be able to put one foot

2652
01:20:18.959 --> 01:20:19.792
in front of the other.

2653
01:20:19.792 --> 01:20:20.967
First, I didn't call majority this time.

2654
01:20:20.967 --> 01:20:24.170
So, when you get up in a warm RV, you do not wanna get out.

2655
01:20:24.170 --> 01:20:25.449
Literally am like, I don't wanna go.

2656
01:20:25.449 --> 01:20:26.792
I would get up.

2657
01:20:26.792 --> 01:20:27.922
This is the time I actually, I guess,

2658
01:20:27.922 --> 01:20:29.778
when you asked the question have you had your breaking point

2659
01:20:29.778 --> 01:20:31.824
where you just, I would just talk to Belle,

2660
01:20:31.824 --> 01:20:33.260
I'm like, "I don't wanna go."

2661
01:20:33.260 --> 01:20:34.651
When I'm saying that, I'm not even joking.

2662
01:20:34.651 --> 01:20:36.172
I'm like, "I don't wanna go.

2663
01:20:36.172 --> 01:20:37.005
I can't do this.

2664
01:20:37.005 --> 01:20:37.838
I don't wanna do."

2665
01:20:37.838 --> 01:20:38.931
I keep repeating it.

2666
01:20:38.931 --> 01:20:40.224
And then I would say, "Hellah, stop, wait a minute.

2667
01:20:40.224 --> 01:20:41.845
Because he keeps saying this,

2668
01:20:41.845 --> 01:20:43.104
your mind is just gonna keep believing.

2669
01:20:43.104 --> 01:20:44.946
Your body's gonna react to it."

2670
01:20:44.946 --> 01:20:46.288
But a lot of the morning, I just get up,

2671
01:20:46.288 --> 01:20:48.242
I'm just like, "I don't wanna do this.

2672
01:20:48.242 --> 01:20:49.357
I don't wanna go."

2673
01:20:49.357 --> 01:20:50.598
And I'm like Soles4Souls.

2674
01:20:50.598 --> 01:20:51.951
Soles4Souls.

2675
01:20:51.951 --> 01:20:53.556
Then I keep repeating that in my head.

2676
01:20:53.556 --> 01:20:56.032
But getting out of the RV was the toughest.

2677
01:20:56.032 --> 01:20:59.134
And even the hardest part after that,

2678
01:20:59.134 --> 01:21:02.025
when Belle brings me to where I dropped the pin,

2679
01:21:02.025 --> 01:21:03.054
where we ended the run.

2680
01:21:03.054 --> 01:21:06.763
And I was always make a sign and put arrow NYC

2681
01:21:06.763 --> 01:21:08.086
and we see a street.

2682
01:21:08.086 --> 01:21:10.947
If I finished my miles and I don't see any street,

2683
01:21:10.947 --> 01:21:12.276
I keep going until I see the next street sign

2684
01:21:12.276 --> 01:21:15.113
and we drop a pin just to make sure we're there.

2685
01:21:15.113 --> 01:21:17.962
When she brings me to drop me off there, the next morning,

2686
01:21:17.962 --> 01:21:20.608
getting out of that, leaving the warm car,

2687
01:21:20.608 --> 01:21:21.997
I like, I wanna cry. (laughs)

2688
01:21:21.997 --> 01:21:23.621
(Rich laughs)

2689
01:21:23.621 --> 01:21:25.399
But as soon as it started going,

2690
01:21:25.399 --> 01:21:27.301
then you're like, "Okay, this is not too bad."

2691
01:21:27.301 --> 01:21:29.655
But that was the hardest, to get up and get out.

2692
01:21:29.655 --> 01:21:33.025
Was there one specific low moment that sticks out?

2693
01:21:33.025 --> 01:21:35.025
Like your lowest moment that almost break you?

2694
01:21:35.025 --> 01:21:36.405
Two lowest moments for me

2695
01:21:36.405 --> 01:21:38.358
was the first full day in Arizona.

2696
01:21:38.358 --> 01:21:40.194
I got into Arizona at a later day,

2697
01:21:40.194 --> 01:21:41.910
where that night I finished.

2698
01:21:41.910 --> 01:21:44.982
But the first full day in Arizona, it was a switchback.

2699
01:21:44.982 --> 01:21:49.350
And I gained 3000 feet in six miles, which is really weird.

2700
01:21:49.350 --> 01:21:50.255
Think about that.

2701
01:21:50.255 --> 01:21:51.564
3000 feet in six miles.

2702
01:21:51.564 --> 01:21:52.785
Yeah, yeah.

2703
01:21:52.785 --> 01:21:53.618
How is that possible?

2704
01:21:53.618 --> 01:21:54.451
Yeah, that's a lot of game.

2705
01:21:54.451 --> 01:21:55.284
Yeah.

2706
01:21:55.284 --> 01:21:56.117
And then it was, so, the goal,

2707
01:21:56.117 --> 01:21:59.123
the thing was mentality for me is fall off the cliff

2708
01:21:59.123 --> 01:22:00.173
or get hit by a car.

2709
01:22:00.173 --> 01:22:02.378
That was like the only two options for me.

2710
01:22:02.378 --> 01:22:03.211
I felt like it was.

2711
01:22:03.211 --> 01:22:04.057
And it really was

2712
01:22:04.057 --> 01:22:06.798
until we had to put me in front of Belle's car

2713
01:22:06.798 --> 01:22:09.257
and she was holding up traffic, and I'm just in front of it.

2714
01:22:09.257 --> 01:22:10.090
If you can get around,

2715
01:22:10.090 --> 01:22:10.969
when you have the opportunity, go ahead.

2716
01:22:10.969 --> 01:22:12.395
If not, you're gonna have to wait.

2717
01:22:12.395 --> 01:22:15.361
Like having her go at six miles an hour in front of me.

2718
01:22:15.361 --> 01:22:17.097
So, as I switched back in Arizona,

2719
01:22:17.097 --> 01:22:19.535
where I'm just climbing and there's this cliff.

2720
01:22:19.535 --> 01:22:21.839
You see cars that fell off of this cliff.

2721
01:22:21.839 --> 01:22:22.995
You see them there.

2722
01:22:22.995 --> 01:22:24.132
Like old cars, rusted-

2723
01:22:24.132 --> 01:22:25.032
Down the Ravine?

2724
01:22:25.032 --> 01:22:27.200
I don't even remember the mountain name.

2725
01:22:27.200 --> 01:22:29.266
I can't believe I can't think of it right now.

2726
01:22:29.266 --> 01:22:30.719
But it was our first day.

2727
01:22:30.719 --> 01:22:31.980
And we keep climbing and I went through everything.

2728
01:22:31.980 --> 01:22:36.509
I went through rain, I went through hail, snow, wind.

2729
01:22:36.509 --> 01:22:39.180
All seasons within that, getting out of that mountain.

2730
01:22:39.180 --> 01:22:42.326
And I was in there for like 13, 14 miles.

2731
01:22:42.326 --> 01:22:45.398
For the first six miles. I think I gained over 3000.

2732
01:22:45.398 --> 01:22:47.390
And it was basically to a point

2733
01:22:47.390 --> 01:22:48.980
where like I felt like I'm going up,

2734
01:22:48.980 --> 01:22:51.875
someone is pulling me back and you're gonna fall backward.

2735
01:22:51.875 --> 01:22:54.890
And you hunch to use your pull to get you up there.

2736
01:22:54.890 --> 01:22:57.774
And the cars, it was dangerous for her, even with a car.

2737
01:22:57.774 --> 01:22:59.644
And I see these cars coming down.

2738
01:22:59.644 --> 01:23:01.808
And you can see cars on top.

2739
01:23:01.808 --> 01:23:02.950
Like, it looked like a stairs.

2740
01:23:02.950 --> 01:23:04.199
How did they get up there?

2741
01:23:04.199 --> 01:23:05.997
And you just see how steep it is.

2742
01:23:05.997 --> 01:23:08.224
And we Google it, why do they have switchbacks?

2743
01:23:08.224 --> 01:23:09.516
That's even to help with elevation.

2744
01:23:09.516 --> 01:23:10.534
That how tough that is.

2745
01:23:10.534 --> 01:23:11.799
Yeah, it is too steep to go straight up.

2746
01:23:11.799 --> 01:23:13.733
Yeah, I killed my knee really like-

2747
01:23:13.733 --> 01:23:15.728
Is that when you were still trying to run the hills?

2748
01:23:15.728 --> 01:23:17.053
Yeah, I was still in the running.

2749
01:23:17.053 --> 01:23:18.152
(Rich laughs)

2750
01:23:18.152 --> 01:23:18.985
Yep.

2751
01:23:18.985 --> 01:23:19.987
That's why I did it for me.

2752
01:23:19.987 --> 01:23:23.462
And Missouri, there's a raining day,

2753
01:23:23.462 --> 01:23:27.296
where 15 miles an hour ahead crosswind.

2754
01:23:27.296 --> 01:23:28.619
And I would get out.

2755
01:23:28.619 --> 01:23:30.079
It was freezing cold out.

2756
01:23:30.079 --> 01:23:33.318
I would get like soaked in water in my shoes.

2757
01:23:33.318 --> 01:23:36.385
I can feel puddles in my shoes within two, three minutes.

2758
01:23:36.385 --> 01:23:37.634
And I couldn't move forward.

2759
01:23:37.634 --> 01:23:38.785
I'm trying to progress forward.

2760
01:23:38.785 --> 01:23:39.618
I can't move forward.

2761
01:23:39.618 --> 01:23:41.331
It was very stressful.

2762
01:23:41.331 --> 01:23:42.913
And I would get into the RV to get out,

2763
01:23:42.913 --> 01:23:44.066
'cause I'm shivering to get...

2764
01:23:44.066 --> 01:23:45.661
I can't even get warm by running.

2765
01:23:45.661 --> 01:23:48.175
To get out of my work clothes to get into new clothes,

2766
01:23:48.175 --> 01:23:49.420
which was a bad idea because as soon as I step outside,

2767
01:23:49.420 --> 01:23:51.703
it felt like I didn't even change.

2768
01:23:51.703 --> 01:23:53.113
And that was tough.

2769
01:23:53.113 --> 01:23:54.847
That was like really tough for me.

2770
01:23:54.847 --> 01:23:56.561
That's the day Belle went on Instagram and said,

2771
01:23:56.561 --> 01:23:58.246
"Hey, Hellah is struggling today.

2772
01:23:58.246 --> 01:23:59.262
'Cause I want people to know the reality.

2773
01:23:59.262 --> 01:24:01.309
It's not always sunshine and rainbows.

2774
01:24:01.309 --> 01:24:03.050
If you guys just wanna send him a message,

2775
01:24:03.050 --> 01:24:03.988
he'll probably appreciate it."

2776
01:24:03.988 --> 01:24:06.084
I'm glad she did that because seeing people come in,

2777
01:24:06.084 --> 01:24:07.322
sending me messages is really cool.

2778
01:24:07.322 --> 01:24:09.623
But those two days I'll never forget because that was-

2779
01:24:09.623 --> 01:24:10.456
That's wild enough.

2780
01:24:10.456 --> 01:24:11.640
Yeah, those two days was tough.

2781
01:24:11.640 --> 01:24:13.514
What's the recovery routine?

2782
01:24:13.514 --> 01:24:16.484
You have the NormaTec boots, you have a Theragun,

2783
01:24:16.484 --> 01:24:17.358
or the Hyperice.

2784
01:24:17.358 --> 01:24:21.859
A Hyperice massage gun and the NormaTec boot

2785
01:24:21.859 --> 01:24:22.692
is really nice.

2786
01:24:22.692 --> 01:24:24.812
And I had a machine called Kelvi.

2787
01:24:24.812 --> 01:24:26.144
So, I don't know if you've heard of Kelvi.

2788
01:24:26.144 --> 01:24:26.977
Uh-uh.

2789
01:24:26.977 --> 01:24:27.945
Ooh, I gotta get you hooked to Kelvi.

2790
01:24:27.945 --> 01:24:29.049
What is that?

2791
01:24:29.049 --> 01:24:31.193
So, Kelvi, have you ever heard of Game Ready?

2792
01:24:31.193 --> 01:24:33.979
It's like ice and water, how they wrap your leg.

2793
01:24:33.979 --> 01:24:38.484
So, Kelvi is a machine that can go to 160 degrees

2794
01:24:38.484 --> 01:24:39.916
within two seconds.

2795
01:24:39.916 --> 01:24:43.134
And that can freeze to 39 degrees within four seconds.

2796
01:24:43.134 --> 01:24:43.967
Wow.

2797
01:24:43.967 --> 01:24:44.800
And it can contract-

2798
01:24:44.800 --> 01:24:46.317
So, you alternate back and forth between all them.

2799
01:24:46.317 --> 01:24:47.150
You can do conscious.

2800
01:24:47.150 --> 01:24:49.266
It'll go hot for three minutes, cold for two minutes.

2801
01:24:49.266 --> 01:24:50.657
Or as you can switch the times.

2802
01:24:50.657 --> 01:24:52.759
Or you can just keep it on cold the whole time or hot.

2803
01:24:52.759 --> 01:24:55.031
So, that was really helping me with recovery.

2804
01:24:55.031 --> 01:24:56.397
And every time I checked-

2805
01:24:56.397 --> 01:24:57.747
Are they like boots like NormaTec?

2806
01:24:57.747 --> 01:24:58.687
They're not boots.

2807
01:24:58.687 --> 01:25:01.557
It is like a console and it has like this wrapping

2808
01:25:01.557 --> 01:25:03.423
where you can wrap around your knee or ankle.

2809
01:25:03.423 --> 01:25:05.026
So, it's completely different than NormaTec.

2810
01:25:05.026 --> 01:25:07.789
But every time I actually did NormaTec, I felt it.

2811
01:25:07.789 --> 01:25:09.199
Every time I didn't put it on I'm like,

2812
01:25:09.199 --> 01:25:10.171
"Why did you do this, Hellah?

2813
01:25:10.171 --> 01:25:12.585
You know when you don't do it, you you're paying for it.

2814
01:25:12.585 --> 01:25:13.702
So, many nights when I-

2815
01:25:13.702 --> 01:25:14.546
These things work.

2816
01:25:14.546 --> 01:25:15.379
It works.

2817
01:25:15.379 --> 01:25:16.212
It's magic.

2818
01:25:16.212 --> 01:25:17.093
It feels like you have a new leg.

2819
01:25:17.093 --> 01:25:20.214
So, I had this time in the day at 2:00 PM, 2:30,

2820
01:25:20.214 --> 01:25:21.507
where I put on normal tech.

2821
01:25:21.507 --> 01:25:23.460
So, that's when I really cruise from 36 miles

2822
01:25:23.460 --> 01:25:24.729
all the way to 47.

2823
01:25:24.729 --> 01:25:25.768
Sometimes I would do that.

2824
01:25:25.768 --> 01:25:28.744
I've done that many times actually nonstop without breaking.

2825
01:25:28.744 --> 01:25:30.896
I would just go straight for it from 36 to 47

2826
01:25:30.896 --> 01:25:31.776
to call my day.

2827
01:25:31.776 --> 01:25:32.609
Yeah.

2828
01:25:32.609 --> 01:25:35.233
But more often than not, taking a NormaTec break

2829
01:25:35.233 --> 01:25:37.673
in the middle of the day for a little reboot.

2830
01:25:37.673 --> 01:25:38.919
Yeah, it's a huge reboot.

2831
01:25:38.919 --> 01:25:39.752
It really is.

2832
01:25:39.752 --> 01:25:42.974
So, I was so happy that I had that to my availability.

2833
01:25:42.974 --> 01:25:45.416
So, now that you have this in the rear view mirror,

2834
01:25:45.416 --> 01:25:49.614
like what else did you learn about human possibility?

2835
01:25:49.614 --> 01:25:53.947
Like where did your mind change from before to after

2836
01:25:55.430 --> 01:25:57.060
in terms of how you see yourself

2837
01:25:57.060 --> 01:26:00.838
and how you kind of think about possibility in general?

2838
01:26:00.838 --> 01:26:03.083
So, I always, like sometime we sit there

2839
01:26:03.083 --> 01:26:05.368
and be like, "Wait, I just ran across the country."

2840
01:26:05.368 --> 01:26:07.302
So, it hasn't gotten old to me.

2841
01:26:07.302 --> 01:26:08.462
I hope it doesn't.

2842
01:26:08.462 --> 01:26:11.277
You just kind of realize that we're not limited.

2843
01:26:11.277 --> 01:26:14.103
And I think of Eliud Kipchoge when he said,

2844
01:26:14.103 --> 01:26:16.231
he still says that no human is limited,

2845
01:26:16.231 --> 01:26:18.245
and sometime like, yeah, we're not limited.

2846
01:26:18.245 --> 01:26:20.499
And I truly believe that because you find your limit

2847
01:26:20.499 --> 01:26:21.332
and you break it.

2848
01:26:21.332 --> 01:26:23.934
I cannot run Eliud Kipchoge marathon time.

2849
01:26:23.934 --> 01:26:26.150
It took him 20-some years to get there.

2850
01:26:26.150 --> 01:26:27.399
But I have my limit,

2851
01:26:27.399 --> 01:26:29.689
but I can break that and find another limit.

2852
01:26:29.689 --> 01:26:31.521
If I wanna do that, I have to spend years on it.

2853
01:26:31.521 --> 01:26:34.220
So, it really reinforced that we are not limited.

2854
01:26:34.220 --> 01:26:36.263
We have a limit right now within ourselves,

2855
01:26:36.263 --> 01:26:37.553
but we can reach that and breakthrough

2856
01:26:37.553 --> 01:26:38.883
and find the next limit.

2857
01:26:38.883 --> 01:26:40.223
So, I feel like I found my limit doing this

2858
01:26:40.223 --> 01:26:41.663
and I broke through it

2859
01:26:41.663 --> 01:26:43.781
because it was time where I thought it was impossible.

2860
01:26:43.781 --> 01:26:46.828
I even thought a hundred days was not even enough for me.

2861
01:26:46.828 --> 01:26:48.095
And then I broke through that limit

2862
01:26:48.095 --> 01:26:50.965
and now it makes me think that I can do other things.

2863
01:26:50.965 --> 01:26:52.290
So, I wanna do Leadville 100.

2864
01:26:52.290 --> 01:26:53.988
That's the next thing?

2865
01:26:53.988 --> 01:26:55.050
I wanna do that.

2866
01:26:55.050 --> 01:26:56.388
And I'm gonna actually trench.

2867
01:26:56.388 --> 01:26:58.528
Are you gonna show up on August 21st when Robbie-

2868
01:26:58.528 --> 01:27:01.400
I feel like that might be a little too soon. (laughs)

2869
01:27:01.400 --> 01:27:03.705
My body is not still there yet,

2870
01:27:03.705 --> 01:27:06.651
but I wanna focus my time actually go in the mountains

2871
01:27:06.651 --> 01:27:07.484
and train.

2872
01:27:07.484 --> 01:27:10.265
So, it really makes you feel like we are much stronger

2873
01:27:10.265 --> 01:27:11.746
than we think we are.

2874
01:27:11.746 --> 01:27:13.322
And whenever you think you are strong as this,

2875
01:27:13.322 --> 01:27:14.622
you're stronger than even that.

2876
01:27:14.622 --> 01:27:16.569
So, if I'm thinking I can do this,

2877
01:27:16.569 --> 01:27:17.810
I can even go beyond that.

2878
01:27:17.810 --> 01:27:19.017
Just always think even beyond that,

2879
01:27:19.017 --> 01:27:20.483
because you'll be able to do it.

2880
01:27:20.483 --> 01:27:22.605
Even if it takes a little longer than someone else has done

2881
01:27:22.605 --> 01:27:23.438
and whatever,

2882
01:27:23.438 --> 01:27:25.553
but you'll be able to find the power

2883
01:27:25.553 --> 01:27:26.777
and the will to get through it.

2884
01:27:26.777 --> 01:27:29.334
Just like the Iron Cowboy doing 101.

2885
01:27:29.334 --> 01:27:30.167
Incredible.

2886
01:27:30.167 --> 01:27:31.192
I cannot wait to meet James.

2887
01:27:31.192 --> 01:27:33.068
I wanna ask him some questions

2888
01:27:33.068 --> 01:27:35.232
and things like that staff they're doing.

2889
01:27:35.232 --> 01:27:36.065
I'll introduce you to him.

2890
01:27:36.065 --> 01:27:36.898
Yeah.

2891
01:27:36.898 --> 01:27:39.141
Talk to me about the mantra that's on the t-shirts

2892
01:27:39.141 --> 01:27:39.974
and the...

2893
01:27:39.974 --> 01:27:40.807
I wanna talk about the bus. (laughs)

2894
01:27:40.807 --> 01:27:43.080
Yeah, that was really cool.

2895
01:27:43.080 --> 01:27:46.352
This phrase, no matter the circumstances,

2896
01:27:46.352 --> 01:27:47.185
what is that about?

2897
01:27:47.185 --> 01:27:48.789
Like, why did you hone in on that

2898
01:27:48.789 --> 01:27:52.536
being that kind of like the touchstone

2899
01:27:52.536 --> 01:27:54.497
or the moniker for the adventure?

2900
01:27:54.497 --> 01:27:56.284
So, when I my run streak, I said,

2901
01:27:56.284 --> 01:27:58.452
"You're gonna go outside and run 10 minutes a day,

2902
01:27:58.452 --> 01:27:59.952
no matter the circumstances."

2903
01:27:59.952 --> 01:28:02.790
Whether that's the weather, whatever it is issue I had.

2904
01:28:02.790 --> 01:28:04.039
I was still having a 9:00 to 5:00.

2905
01:28:04.039 --> 01:28:06.086
You wanna get up early and run before work,

2906
01:28:06.086 --> 01:28:06.919
or you wanna run after work.

2907
01:28:06.919 --> 01:28:09.426
So, circumstances are gonna prevent you

2908
01:28:09.426 --> 01:28:10.558
from getting out there.

2909
01:28:10.558 --> 01:28:13.370
So, the mentality was no matter the circumstances

2910
01:28:13.370 --> 01:28:14.708
from LA to New York City,

2911
01:28:14.708 --> 01:28:16.570
whatever happened, you gotta make it happen.

2912
01:28:16.570 --> 01:28:18.405
And to a point I was thinking,

2913
01:28:18.405 --> 01:28:21.509
even if I have to crawl like a baby on my hands and knees,

2914
01:28:21.509 --> 01:28:22.831
if that's the only way I'm gonna move forward,

2915
01:28:22.831 --> 01:28:25.464
it might take 200 days now, but I have to make it happen.

2916
01:28:25.464 --> 01:28:27.654
So, that's where no matter the circumstances,

2917
01:28:27.654 --> 01:28:29.028
I wanted to preach that to everybody.

2918
01:28:29.028 --> 01:28:30.278
Every single day, I said,

2919
01:28:30.278 --> 01:28:32.572
because if we wanna do something, we can make it happen.

2920
01:28:32.572 --> 01:28:35.526
So, we just gotta push through whatever circumstances

2921
01:28:35.526 --> 01:28:36.575
come our way, good or bad.

2922
01:28:36.575 --> 01:28:38.817
Because circumstances doesn't always have to be bad.

2923
01:28:38.817 --> 01:28:40.246
It could be like, "Oh, I'm at a party."

2924
01:28:40.246 --> 01:28:42.258
It's a great circumstance right now.

2925
01:28:42.258 --> 01:28:43.103
(Rich laughs)

2926
01:28:43.103 --> 01:28:44.156
But you gotta get your work in,

2927
01:28:44.156 --> 01:28:44.989
no matter the circumstances,

2928
01:28:44.989 --> 01:28:47.150
you gotta get out there and push through.

2929
01:28:47.150 --> 01:28:48.547
Have you always been this guy

2930
01:28:48.547 --> 01:28:50.489
who's inspiring everybody around him?

2931
01:28:50.489 --> 01:28:52.424
Did you mature into this?

2932
01:28:52.424 --> 01:28:54.253
And when you were a kid, were you like this?

2933
01:28:54.253 --> 01:28:55.268
Where does this come from?

2934
01:28:55.268 --> 01:28:57.855
I think the fact that I grew up in West Africa,

2935
01:28:57.855 --> 01:28:59.807
I really quickly grasp on,

2936
01:28:59.807 --> 01:29:03.069
I have a really good, I have my best friends' kids,

2937
01:29:03.069 --> 01:29:04.354
my age that are in Africa that'd do anything

2938
01:29:04.354 --> 01:29:05.686
to be in my position.

2939
01:29:05.686 --> 01:29:08.775
So, what's not there to be happy when in life?

2940
01:29:08.775 --> 01:29:10.184
Like to me right now, what is life?

2941
01:29:10.184 --> 01:29:13.349
I'm sitting across from the Rich Roll talking.

2942
01:29:13.349 --> 01:29:17.028
So, there's little moments in my life that I think about

2943
01:29:17.028 --> 01:29:19.200
or major moments in my life that I think about,

2944
01:29:19.200 --> 01:29:21.242
no matter I'm going through any little tough time and say,

2945
01:29:21.242 --> 01:29:24.075
"Come on, Hellah, just a time frame that's gonna go by."

2946
01:29:24.075 --> 01:29:26.612
So, what really makes me push through anything

2947
01:29:26.612 --> 01:29:27.861
and just always have a smile on,

2948
01:29:27.861 --> 01:29:30.745
when there was times where I was really struggling,

2949
01:29:30.745 --> 01:29:32.019
nothing was going my way,

2950
01:29:32.019 --> 01:29:33.430
and I thought that was the end of everything.

2951
01:29:33.430 --> 01:29:35.671
I really thought like your future is done.

2952
01:29:35.671 --> 01:29:37.502
You have nothing to look forward to.

2953
01:29:37.502 --> 01:29:38.572
And I'm sitting here.

2954
01:29:38.572 --> 01:29:40.545
So, whenever I go through a tough time, I just laugh.

2955
01:29:40.545 --> 01:29:43.001
I say, "Remember that one time you thought this is it?

2956
01:29:43.001 --> 01:29:43.834
Look at that."

2957
01:29:43.834 --> 01:29:44.777
And vividly actually,

2958
01:29:44.777 --> 01:29:48.000
when I signed my first professional contract in 2013,

2959
01:29:48.000 --> 01:29:49.919
as a professional, you get paid, right?

2960
01:29:49.919 --> 01:29:52.860
So, imagine a professional that is signing a contract,

2961
01:29:52.860 --> 01:29:55.098
has no money in his bank account even to eat.

2962
01:29:55.098 --> 01:29:58.315
And you don't have the got to reach out

2963
01:29:58.315 --> 01:29:59.682
to family members, to friends.

2964
01:29:59.682 --> 01:30:01.767
How are you gonna ask for money to go get groceries?

2965
01:30:01.767 --> 01:30:03.628
You just signed a professional contract.

2966
01:30:03.628 --> 01:30:05.665
So, I remember one day playing in Seattle.

2967
01:30:05.665 --> 01:30:07.188
I have a game coming up.

2968
01:30:07.188 --> 01:30:08.265
And I want to buy food.

2969
01:30:08.265 --> 01:30:09.139
My card was declined.

2970
01:30:09.139 --> 01:30:11.255
So, I get home and I look at my bank account.

2971
01:30:11.255 --> 01:30:12.678
I was $0.

2972
01:30:12.678 --> 01:30:14.893
So, I didn't know what to do.

2973
01:30:14.893 --> 01:30:16.734
So, I called my bank, I said,

2974
01:30:16.734 --> 01:30:18.918
"Hey, can you guys allow me to overdraft?

2975
01:30:18.918 --> 01:30:20.258
I will get paid in two weeks."

2976
01:30:20.258 --> 01:30:22.089
'Cause they would pass biweekly.

2977
01:30:22.089 --> 01:30:23.911
"And I just wanna overdraft.

2978
01:30:23.911 --> 01:30:24.984
You can charge me the fee."

2979
01:30:24.984 --> 01:30:26.779
And then the lady that was with me said,

2980
01:30:26.779 --> 01:30:28.108
"No, I can't do that for you."

2981
01:30:28.108 --> 01:30:30.598
So I said, "Please, just allow me to do this."

2982
01:30:30.598 --> 01:30:31.901
And she said, "Let me connect to the manager."

2983
01:30:31.901 --> 01:30:33.327
So, the manager came on

2984
01:30:33.327 --> 01:30:35.030
and I wish I can find who he is today.

2985
01:30:35.030 --> 01:30:35.863
But I talked to him.

2986
01:30:35.863 --> 01:30:37.565
He goes, "I'm not gonna allow you to overdraft."

2987
01:30:37.565 --> 01:30:38.398
He said, "You know why?

2988
01:30:38.398 --> 01:30:39.585
Because if I allowed you to overdraft,

2989
01:30:39.585 --> 01:30:40.967
what happens if you don't pay?

2990
01:30:40.967 --> 01:30:41.800
The fee adds up.

2991
01:30:41.800 --> 01:30:43.065
Next thing you know, you're gonna be negative

2992
01:30:43.065 --> 01:30:43.898
and owe a lot of money."

2993
01:30:43.898 --> 01:30:44.731
And he said, "You know what I'll do?

2994
01:30:44.731 --> 01:30:47.374
I'll give you $30 credit right now so you can go get food."

2995
01:30:47.374 --> 01:30:49.811
So, I go get a week worth of groceries.

2996
01:30:49.811 --> 01:30:51.935
Like Aldi was cheap store.

2997
01:30:51.935 --> 01:30:54.231
And I think about that day,

2998
01:30:54.231 --> 01:30:56.264
because that day I was really like,

2999
01:30:56.264 --> 01:30:58.901
I'm an athlete I have to perform, but I didn't have food.

3000
01:30:58.901 --> 01:31:00.178
I couldn't even ask my teammates.

3001
01:31:00.178 --> 01:31:05.178
And so, thinking back to all those times, nothing really,

3002
01:31:05.715 --> 01:31:07.721
adds more to you just wanna smile

3003
01:31:07.721 --> 01:31:09.800
because I really have it good.

3004
01:31:09.800 --> 01:31:12.666
I'm able to run every day, realizing my dream,

3005
01:31:12.666 --> 01:31:14.603
which is running every day.

3006
01:31:14.603 --> 01:31:15.492
It's a privilege of mine.

3007
01:31:15.492 --> 01:31:16.325
I have two legs.

3008
01:31:16.325 --> 01:31:17.158
I have two limbs.

3009
01:31:17.158 --> 01:31:18.532
And even running every day is a privilege

3010
01:31:18.532 --> 01:31:20.946
because there's people who can't walk, let alone run.

3011
01:31:20.946 --> 01:31:23.054
And in the back of my mind, I'm doing it for them too.

3012
01:31:23.054 --> 01:31:24.297
It's not about me anymore.

3013
01:31:24.297 --> 01:31:26.538
So, I can't do anything, but be happy.

3014
01:31:26.538 --> 01:31:27.371
Be excited.

3015
01:31:27.371 --> 01:31:28.204
And it's life.

3016
01:31:28.204 --> 01:31:29.728
Life is really beautiful.

3017
01:31:29.728 --> 01:31:31.498
Even though we have these little bumps along the way,

3018
01:31:31.498 --> 01:31:34.321
but overall, having people around you, family, friends,

3019
01:31:34.321 --> 01:31:36.922
and having because of social media, I have a big family now.

3020
01:31:36.922 --> 01:31:38.889
'Cause I'm like I have now all these people

3021
01:31:38.889 --> 01:31:39.842
around the world.

3022
01:31:39.842 --> 01:31:40.675
Cool people.

3023
01:31:40.675 --> 01:31:42.663
I know you, I know James now.

3024
01:31:42.663 --> 01:31:43.645
I know all these incredible.

3025
01:31:43.645 --> 01:31:44.925
It's just, you can not smile.

3026
01:31:44.925 --> 01:31:46.122
You really can't.

3027
01:31:46.122 --> 01:31:47.022
That's beautiful, man.

3028
01:31:47.022 --> 01:31:48.472
I love the gratitude and the appreciation.

3029
01:31:48.472 --> 01:31:49.878
Thank you. Yeah.

3030
01:31:49.878 --> 01:31:52.520
It's very infectious.

3031
01:31:52.520 --> 01:31:53.353
Thank you.

3032
01:31:53.353 --> 01:31:54.186
Yeah.

3033
01:31:54.186 --> 01:31:58.612
Does the village back in Mali know what you've been doing?

3034
01:31:58.612 --> 01:31:59.445
Yeah.

3035
01:31:59.445 --> 01:32:00.379
Like have you talked to anybody back there?

3036
01:32:00.379 --> 01:32:01.684
Actually, yeah.

3037
01:32:01.684 --> 01:32:06.613
So, the funny thing is my dad actually forbid me to run.

3038
01:32:06.613 --> 01:32:08.279
He told me, he said, "Hellah, I forbid you to run?

3039
01:32:08.279 --> 01:32:09.364
What is this run nonsense?"

3040
01:32:09.364 --> 01:32:10.197
(Rich laughs)

3041
01:32:10.197 --> 01:32:11.030
He said that to me.

3042
01:32:11.030 --> 01:32:11.863
He literally said, what is this-

3043
01:32:11.863 --> 01:32:12.821
How old were you when he told you that?

3044
01:32:12.821 --> 01:32:14.875
He told me this in 2018 running

3045
01:32:14.875 --> 01:32:16.968
when I was just two years in.

3046
01:32:16.968 --> 01:32:20.254
'Cause I went back to Mali and I was still running.

3047
01:32:20.254 --> 01:32:21.111
My sister was getting married.

3048
01:32:21.111 --> 01:32:22.877
I was so good at my running.

3049
01:32:22.877 --> 01:32:23.710
And he said, you're gonna...

3050
01:32:23.710 --> 01:32:27.605
He was sending me videos of people dropping dead

3051
01:32:27.605 --> 01:32:29.823
in soccer matches.

3052
01:32:29.823 --> 01:32:32.186
And then he said, "This is what running will do to you."

3053
01:32:32.186 --> 01:32:33.962
And it's funny because he was the biggest supporter

3054
01:32:33.962 --> 01:32:35.329
for me to play professional soccer.

3055
01:32:35.329 --> 01:32:37.242
So, I said, "Dad, what's the difference?

3056
01:32:37.242 --> 01:32:38.490
Those professional soccer,

3057
01:32:38.490 --> 01:32:39.465
if I was playing professionally,

3058
01:32:39.465 --> 01:32:40.372
would you say the same thing?

3059
01:32:40.372 --> 01:32:41.736
Because I'm still running.

3060
01:32:41.736 --> 01:32:44.499
It's just that maybe you like one versus the other."

3061
01:32:44.499 --> 01:32:47.463
And he basically told me, "I want you to stop this running,"

3062
01:32:47.463 --> 01:32:48.514
since he never was supportive.

3063
01:32:48.514 --> 01:32:50.766
And my mom was more like I'm concerned for my child.

3064
01:32:50.766 --> 01:32:52.046
Don't hurt yourself kinda thing.

3065
01:32:52.046 --> 01:32:53.921
But things turned around.

3066
01:32:53.921 --> 01:32:55.852
And then my little brother would said,

3067
01:32:55.852 --> 01:32:57.449
"Dad, I think Hellah is doing something

3068
01:32:57.449 --> 01:33:01.135
that is gonna be great because he's doing it for himself

3069
01:33:01.135 --> 01:33:02.445
and other things."

3070
01:33:02.445 --> 01:33:05.343
So, now he's one of the biggest support.

3071
01:33:05.343 --> 01:33:06.934
He said, "Hellah, now I understand."

3072
01:33:06.934 --> 01:33:09.604
He was so proud of the whole run across the country.

3073
01:33:09.604 --> 01:33:10.706
He was so happy about it.

3074
01:33:10.706 --> 01:33:14.614
In fact, he wrote a note to have my sister read it

3075
01:33:14.614 --> 01:33:15.624
at the finish.

3076
01:33:15.624 --> 01:33:18.718
And basically saying, "I have three PhDs."

3077
01:33:18.718 --> 01:33:23.710
My grandfather, Hellah, that's who I was named after,

3078
01:33:23.710 --> 01:33:25.186
he said he was a peasant,

3079
01:33:25.186 --> 01:33:27.641
but he find a way to get out of the situation

3080
01:33:27.641 --> 01:33:30.486
and make himself who he was before he passed.

3081
01:33:30.486 --> 01:33:31.722
And then he said, "You top all of us.

3082
01:33:31.722 --> 01:33:32.604
You ran across the country."

3083
01:33:32.604 --> 01:33:33.790
And he said, "May the legend continue."

3084
01:33:33.790 --> 01:33:35.662
Now he's like one of the biggest support.

3085
01:33:35.662 --> 01:33:36.508
He goes, "Now I get it."

3086
01:33:36.508 --> 01:33:37.419
And he goes,

3087
01:33:37.419 --> 01:33:38.669
"I don't even know where you got the genetic from

3088
01:33:38.669 --> 01:33:39.890
'cause it's not for me.

3089
01:33:39.890 --> 01:33:41.102
'Cause I can't run this much."

3090
01:33:41.102 --> 01:33:43.055
He couldn't believe that I was doing that many.

3091
01:33:43.055 --> 01:33:46.107
We're talking about at 1.75 kilometer in kilometers a day.

3092
01:33:46.107 --> 01:33:47.760
So, now he's fully behind it.

3093
01:33:47.760 --> 01:33:49.927
But now the whole country,

3094
01:33:50.800 --> 01:33:53.884
basically most of the people that I know in Mali

3095
01:33:53.884 --> 01:33:55.095
are like, "Wow, this is incredible."

3096
01:33:55.095 --> 01:33:57.828
But the biggest part for me

3097
01:33:57.828 --> 01:33:59.103
to have like kind of an understanding

3098
01:33:59.103 --> 01:34:02.428
and not even have to be supportive, just understanding,

3099
01:34:02.428 --> 01:34:03.353
was my dad.

3100
01:34:03.353 --> 01:34:04.710
And now he's all about it.

3101
01:34:04.710 --> 01:34:05.607
That's cool.

3102
01:34:05.607 --> 01:34:07.698
Well, given that he was such a tough sell,

3103
01:34:07.698 --> 01:34:08.891
it's all the more meaningful, right?

3104
01:34:08.891 --> 01:34:10.756
Yeah, he was not about it at all.

3105
01:34:10.756 --> 01:34:11.873
He was not, yeah.

3106
01:34:11.873 --> 01:34:12.706
(Rich laughs)

3107
01:34:12.706 --> 01:34:13.575
But now it's completely different.

3108
01:34:13.575 --> 01:34:16.173
He's always saying like, "Oh this is awesome.

3109
01:34:16.173 --> 01:34:17.006
Proud of you."

3110
01:34:17.006 --> 01:34:19.043
And then he's like, "I saw this article."

3111
01:34:19.043 --> 01:34:21.031
So, now he kinda see the bigger picture

3112
01:34:21.031 --> 01:34:24.050
that I always had a vision to do something for others

3113
01:34:24.050 --> 01:34:25.062
and not just about me.

3114
01:34:25.062 --> 01:34:26.006
And now he can see that.

3115
01:34:26.006 --> 01:34:27.680
He wasn't sold on the YouTube thing either.

3116
01:34:27.680 --> 01:34:28.948
Oh yeah, YouTube, no.

3117
01:34:28.948 --> 01:34:30.806
(Rich laughs)

3118
01:34:30.806 --> 01:34:32.185
In French, they say mannequin.

3119
01:34:32.185 --> 01:34:33.351
Mannequin is basically like a model.

3120
01:34:33.351 --> 01:34:36.042
He said, "What is this modeling stuff you're doing?

3121
01:34:36.042 --> 01:34:37.438
Showing your body, running on YouTube.

3122
01:34:37.438 --> 01:34:38.619
What is that?

3123
01:34:38.619 --> 01:34:39.798
What is that gonna do for you?"

3124
01:34:39.798 --> 01:34:40.744
Yeah, he wasn't about that too.

3125
01:34:40.744 --> 01:34:43.593
Now he binge watched my YouTube videos. (laughs)

3126
01:34:43.593 --> 01:34:45.019
(laughs) That's great.

3127
01:34:45.019 --> 01:34:46.304
Yeah.

3128
01:34:46.304 --> 01:34:47.233
Even I'd make fun of my sister.

3129
01:34:47.233 --> 01:34:48.106
There's no hard feelings at all.

3130
01:34:48.106 --> 01:34:49.379
So, my sister, the reason I'm telling this story

3131
01:34:49.379 --> 01:34:52.044
is because people are not gonna support you.

3132
01:34:52.044 --> 01:34:53.267
Even the closest ones to you

3133
01:34:53.267 --> 01:34:55.330
are not gonna understand what you're trying to do.

3134
01:34:55.330 --> 01:34:58.804
My sister told me this, Fadima, she's listening to this.

3135
01:34:58.804 --> 01:34:59.819
She knows it's all love.

3136
01:34:59.819 --> 01:35:00.715
I love her.

3137
01:35:00.715 --> 01:35:02.403
But I was joking around with her.

3138
01:35:02.403 --> 01:35:03.700
She told me, "Why don't you stop this stupid YouTube thing

3139
01:35:03.700 --> 01:35:04.894
and get a real job?"

3140
01:35:04.894 --> 01:35:06.484
She said that to me one day.

3141
01:35:06.484 --> 01:35:07.799
It really hurt because you're like, man,

3142
01:35:07.799 --> 01:35:09.572
this is someone that's closest to you.

3143
01:35:09.572 --> 01:35:13.408
And then I was able to get my plane ticket,

3144
01:35:13.408 --> 01:35:15.736
to go to her wedding, which is like a last-minute notice.

3145
01:35:15.736 --> 01:35:17.350
It was a month before.

3146
01:35:17.350 --> 01:35:20.092
"I'm getting married in Mali, can you come?"

3147
01:35:20.092 --> 01:35:22.391
I used the YouTube money that we had.

3148
01:35:22.391 --> 01:35:23.224
It was not mine.

3149
01:35:23.224 --> 01:35:24.057
It's Belle and I.

3150
01:35:24.057 --> 01:35:24.890
We do this together.

3151
01:35:24.890 --> 01:35:26.030
She said, "Just deposit into your account."

3152
01:35:26.030 --> 01:35:27.287
We've never touched anything from YouTube.

3153
01:35:27.287 --> 01:35:29.238
It was just enough for a plane ticket.

3154
01:35:29.238 --> 01:35:32.170
So, I bought tickets to go to Mali.

3155
01:35:32.170 --> 01:35:33.504
So, when I got to Mali, I was like,

3156
01:35:33.504 --> 01:35:35.262
"Fadima, how sad would've been

3157
01:35:35.262 --> 01:35:36.927
that your own brother couldn't make it to your wedding

3158
01:35:36.927 --> 01:35:37.760
because he couldn't afford it,

3159
01:35:37.760 --> 01:35:39.143
but well, thank God for YouTube." (laughs)

3160
01:35:39.143 --> 01:35:42.320
(Rich laughs)

3161
01:35:42.320 --> 01:35:43.333
Did she come around now too?

3162
01:35:43.333 --> 01:35:45.520
Now she's been super supportive.

3163
01:35:45.520 --> 01:35:47.726
It didn't take long for her to understand.

3164
01:35:47.726 --> 01:35:48.997
That was in the very beginning stage.

3165
01:35:48.997 --> 01:35:50.096
That's cool.

3166
01:35:50.096 --> 01:35:51.427
Yeah, she even came at the finish line with her husband

3167
01:35:51.427 --> 01:35:52.821
and my nephew.

3168
01:35:52.821 --> 01:35:54.064
And you're making it work.

3169
01:35:54.064 --> 01:35:55.214
Yeah.

3170
01:35:55.214 --> 01:35:57.385
In terms of like making a living on YouTube

3171
01:35:57.385 --> 01:35:58.218
and supporting yourself.

3172
01:35:58.218 --> 01:35:59.427
You've got these sponsor relationships.

3173
01:35:59.427 --> 01:36:01.054
Yeah, which is really cool.

3174
01:36:01.054 --> 01:36:01.933
Like I couldn't,

3175
01:36:01.933 --> 01:36:04.337
like even I remember one day actually,

3176
01:36:04.337 --> 01:36:05.638
I was laughing really hard.

3177
01:36:05.638 --> 01:36:08.332
And Belle's looking at me across the road

3178
01:36:08.332 --> 01:36:09.165
during the transcontinent.

3179
01:36:09.165 --> 01:36:09.998
So, she said, "Are you okay?"

3180
01:36:09.998 --> 01:36:10.831
I was like, "I'm just smiling.

3181
01:36:10.831 --> 01:36:11.664
Because look at this.

3182
01:36:11.664 --> 01:36:12.497
What is life?

3183
01:36:12.497 --> 01:36:13.330
We're able to do this?

3184
01:36:13.330 --> 01:36:14.163
We don't have to worry about anything.

3185
01:36:14.163 --> 01:36:15.569
Like we we're good.

3186
01:36:15.569 --> 01:36:16.839
We have food to eat.

3187
01:36:16.839 --> 01:36:18.876
We have a sponsored Gymshark

3188
01:36:18.876 --> 01:36:21.731
that gave us a mobile home, the RV.

3189
01:36:21.731 --> 01:36:25.097
We have a sponsor, Vivo Life, is paying for our food.

3190
01:36:25.097 --> 01:36:26.056
Like this is incredible.

3191
01:36:26.056 --> 01:36:26.889
Why can I not?

3192
01:36:26.889 --> 01:36:28.842
Like I can't just stop smiling about it."

3193
01:36:28.842 --> 01:36:31.480
So, I am grateful to say, because of my sponsors,

3194
01:36:31.480 --> 01:36:32.313
I'm making a living.

3195
01:36:32.313 --> 01:36:33.962
I can do this full-time.

3196
01:36:33.962 --> 01:36:35.210
I can travel around the world

3197
01:36:35.210 --> 01:36:38.175
and we can create content anywhere we go.

3198
01:36:38.175 --> 01:36:41.158
And what I let people understand is it's not even YouTube.

3199
01:36:41.158 --> 01:36:43.429
Because for YouTube, for us, this is the shrift.

3200
01:36:43.429 --> 01:36:46.034
Truth about it, you don't really make enough on YouTube.

3201
01:36:46.034 --> 01:36:46.867
Well, I don't.

3202
01:36:46.867 --> 01:36:48.026
To live, you cannot.

3203
01:36:48.026 --> 01:36:49.428
It's more about because I love.

3204
01:36:49.428 --> 01:36:50.742
There's a lot of illusion around that.

3205
01:36:50.742 --> 01:36:52.022
Yeah. Yeah.

3206
01:36:52.022 --> 01:36:53.291
Like if it was for money in the beginning,

3207
01:36:53.291 --> 01:36:54.642
we would have quit a long time ago.

3208
01:36:54.642 --> 01:36:56.849
It's just, I love sharing my passion with people

3209
01:36:56.849 --> 01:36:58.500
to let them know you can have your own journey,

3210
01:36:58.500 --> 01:37:00.156
whether that's running or not, or anything else,

3211
01:37:00.156 --> 01:37:02.614
and just stick to it and get it done.

3212
01:37:02.614 --> 01:37:04.696
And, but what YouTube did for us

3213
01:37:04.696 --> 01:37:06.670
is brought the opportunity to be signed by Gymshark

3214
01:37:06.670 --> 01:37:09.620
as the second ever runner and to be signed by Vivo Life.

3215
01:37:09.620 --> 01:37:11.003
So, those sponsors allowed you

3216
01:37:11.003 --> 01:37:13.053
to be able to be a little more flexible with yourself

3217
01:37:13.053 --> 01:37:17.006
and at least make a living in terms of you can eat,

3218
01:37:17.006 --> 01:37:18.284
you can have a roof over your head.

3219
01:37:18.284 --> 01:37:19.421
And do the thing.

3220
01:37:19.421 --> 01:37:20.254
Yeah. Yeah.

3221
01:37:20.254 --> 01:37:21.087
Do the thing that you love, right?

3222
01:37:21.087 --> 01:37:21.920
Exactly.

3223
01:37:21.920 --> 01:37:22.753
Those guys showed up for you.

3224
01:37:22.753 --> 01:37:24.727
I mean that bus on the final day, talk about-

3225
01:37:24.727 --> 01:37:26.968
Yeah, Gymshark, he really went all out.

3226
01:37:26.968 --> 01:37:28.817
Go to his Instagram or his YouTube

3227
01:37:28.817 --> 01:37:30.908
and watch the final day.

3228
01:37:30.908 --> 01:37:32.170
I mean, that bus is unbelievable.

3229
01:37:32.170 --> 01:37:33.399
It's a party bus with crazy tunes.

3230
01:37:33.399 --> 01:37:34.251
It's crazy, yeah.

3231
01:37:34.251 --> 01:37:35.524
I mean, like there's people on it

3232
01:37:35.524 --> 01:37:36.825
like riding into the city.

3233
01:37:36.825 --> 01:37:38.097
Yeah, they had the rap all done.

3234
01:37:38.097 --> 01:37:39.658
And they did the RV too.

3235
01:37:39.658 --> 01:37:41.077
The rap, no matter the circumstance.

3236
01:37:41.077 --> 01:37:43.452
And in French also, peu importe les circonstances.

3237
01:37:43.452 --> 01:37:44.771
And they had that whole thing.

3238
01:37:44.771 --> 01:37:47.610
They had a permit to shut a whole street down

3239
01:37:47.610 --> 01:37:48.713
in New York City.

3240
01:37:48.713 --> 01:37:52.637
They had police, NYPD, escort them, warned them to get us.

3241
01:37:52.637 --> 01:37:55.358
And my town really showed up Rochelle Park, New Jersey.

3242
01:37:55.358 --> 01:37:56.306
I had a town mash it up.

3243
01:37:56.306 --> 01:37:57.455
Yeah, whole town.

3244
01:37:57.455 --> 01:37:58.288
The deputy mayor.

3245
01:37:58.288 --> 01:37:59.121
I didn't know that was happening.

3246
01:37:59.121 --> 01:38:00.169
I go around, I'm like, "Wait, is this for me?

3247
01:38:00.169 --> 01:38:01.406
What's going on"

3248
01:38:01.406 --> 01:38:03.874
The firefighter with a big American flag,

3249
01:38:03.874 --> 01:38:05.922
which was a problem for me because no matter what,

3250
01:38:05.922 --> 01:38:08.282
America made me who I am now.

3251
01:38:08.282 --> 01:38:10.694
Because of America, I got the chance

3252
01:38:10.694 --> 01:38:12.914
to me living the American dream.

3253
01:38:12.914 --> 01:38:16.449
Because I came from a place where nothing was very promising

3254
01:38:16.449 --> 01:38:18.325
and now I'm living the American dream.

3255
01:38:18.325 --> 01:38:20.878
So, when I saw that flag, it hit me hard.

3256
01:38:20.878 --> 01:38:21.752
Like a big flag.

3257
01:38:21.752 --> 01:38:24.664
It was like bigger than the whole fire truck.

3258
01:38:24.664 --> 01:38:26.934
They had like a ladder holding it hang down.

3259
01:38:26.934 --> 01:38:28.566
So, seeing the town show up

3260
01:38:28.566 --> 01:38:31.194
and having Gymshark support, Vivo Life support,

3261
01:38:31.194 --> 01:38:33.833
is just, you always think, "Wow, what, this is happening."

3262
01:38:33.833 --> 01:38:36.040
And I was joking with everybody who would arrive.

3263
01:38:36.040 --> 01:38:38.416
I was like, "Should I run across the country again?

3264
01:38:38.416 --> 01:38:39.877
'Cause this is exciting just to see. (laughs)

3265
01:38:39.877 --> 01:38:40.710
(Rich laughs)

3266
01:38:40.710 --> 01:38:41.892
I'm gonna have to do this twice again."

3267
01:38:41.892 --> 01:38:42.809
Yeah. Yeah.

3268
01:38:43.674 --> 01:38:46.155
It was cool seeing you go into Manhattan.

3269
01:38:46.155 --> 01:38:48.549
The roads, were they shut down?

3270
01:38:48.549 --> 01:38:49.947
Like which avenue were you going up

3271
01:38:49.947 --> 01:38:52.724
where it was just a huge perception of you guys in the bus.

3272
01:38:52.724 --> 01:38:55.785
Yeah, so we turned onto second street.

3273
01:38:55.785 --> 01:38:57.563
And then Belle called me and said,

3274
01:38:57.563 --> 01:38:58.576
"We're gonna have a police escort.

3275
01:38:58.576 --> 01:38:59.919
So, keep the left side of the road."

3276
01:38:59.919 --> 01:39:01.384
I was like, "Okay, okay, we'll follow the rules."

3277
01:39:01.384 --> 01:39:02.630
So, we turned and this police officer

3278
01:39:02.630 --> 01:39:05.181
just pulled in front of us with the sirens

3279
01:39:05.181 --> 01:39:07.831
and then slowing like traffic

3280
01:39:07.831 --> 01:39:09.244
like literally opening the road to us.

3281
01:39:09.244 --> 01:39:12.293
So, it just became a whole party literally.

3282
01:39:12.293 --> 01:39:15.789
The music is blasting from the bus that Gymshark had,

3283
01:39:15.789 --> 01:39:16.868
the cutoff top.

3284
01:39:16.868 --> 01:39:17.701
And-

3285
01:39:17.701 --> 01:39:18.534
You're dancing.

3286
01:39:18.534 --> 01:39:19.367
We're dancing.

3287
01:39:19.367 --> 01:39:20.810
Everybody's basically dancing on the road

3288
01:39:20.810 --> 01:39:22.842
'cause we would have to follow now the traffic light.

3289
01:39:22.842 --> 01:39:24.206
So, we get to our traffic light,

3290
01:39:24.206 --> 01:39:26.833
we have to pause the run because the crossroads

3291
01:39:26.833 --> 01:39:28.733
and the police would stop and we'll stop

3292
01:39:28.733 --> 01:39:29.973
and people would start dancing.

3293
01:39:29.973 --> 01:39:31.958
Everybody, bystanders, people like recording.

3294
01:39:31.958 --> 01:39:33.615
People like getting out of their car, like what's going on?

3295
01:39:33.615 --> 01:39:34.877
They don't know what's going on.

3296
01:39:34.877 --> 01:39:36.305
And it was just amazing.

3297
01:39:36.305 --> 01:39:38.557
At one point actually, we took over the whole street.

3298
01:39:38.557 --> 01:39:40.238
No one could even drive on it.

3299
01:39:40.238 --> 01:39:41.071
We stopped at a light.

3300
01:39:41.071 --> 01:39:42.163
I saw the officer,

3301
01:39:42.163 --> 01:39:43.853
the passenger officer comes out of the car,

3302
01:39:43.853 --> 01:39:44.686
I'm like, "Oh, oh, we're in trouble.

3303
01:39:44.686 --> 01:39:46.016
He's gonna probably tell us to keep one side."

3304
01:39:46.016 --> 01:39:47.887
'Cause that's what I was instructed to.

3305
01:39:47.887 --> 01:39:48.772
He comes out with a cigar.

3306
01:39:48.772 --> 01:39:50.669
He goes, "Hey gentlemen, I just wanna let you guys know

3307
01:39:50.669 --> 01:39:52.559
we're about to make a left on 50th street,

3308
01:39:52.559 --> 01:39:53.707
and that's where the finish line is."

3309
01:39:53.707 --> 01:39:54.835
And everybody started shooting

3310
01:39:54.835 --> 01:39:56.294
because we were not in trouble.

3311
01:39:56.294 --> 01:39:58.005
He literally came out, he basically-

3312
01:39:58.005 --> 01:39:58.838
That's New York cops.

3313
01:39:58.838 --> 01:39:59.671
They're the best.

3314
01:39:59.671 --> 01:40:00.504
Literally the best.

3315
01:40:00.504 --> 01:40:01.337
He came out to let us know

3316
01:40:01.337 --> 01:40:03.297
that we're about to get to the finish line.

3317
01:40:03.297 --> 01:40:04.130
And I thought it was

3318
01:40:04.130 --> 01:40:05.784
because we literally took over the whole road.

3319
01:40:05.784 --> 01:40:08.509
It was amazing having everybody come in.

3320
01:40:08.509 --> 01:40:11.417
And when I was doing that last run, I called Robbie.

3321
01:40:11.417 --> 01:40:12.677
I said, "Hey Robbie, I want you to be next to me."

3322
01:40:12.677 --> 01:40:14.321
'Cause I thought it was a full circle.

3323
01:40:14.321 --> 01:40:15.641
I was there for his last day.

3324
01:40:15.641 --> 01:40:17.571
He came out for me and throughout the transcontinental

3325
01:40:17.571 --> 01:40:19.323
and he's there for my last day.

3326
01:40:19.323 --> 01:40:21.197
I said, "Robbie, step up, let's go."

3327
01:40:21.197 --> 01:40:22.183
And then I had Garrett.

3328
01:40:22.183 --> 01:40:23.203
I said, "Garrett, get up here."

3329
01:40:23.203 --> 01:40:24.420
So, Robbie was like, "Garrett, get up."

3330
01:40:24.420 --> 01:40:26.589
You can hear in the audio on the video.

3331
01:40:26.589 --> 01:40:27.840
I just wanted them to be in the front with me

3332
01:40:27.840 --> 01:40:29.614
because it was really special.

3333
01:40:29.614 --> 01:40:32.633
And then for some reason, I found the strength.

3334
01:40:32.633 --> 01:40:34.167
My legs were-

3335
01:40:34.167 --> 01:40:35.429
You looked fresh.

3336
01:40:35.429 --> 01:40:37.170
You did not look tired at all.

3337
01:40:37.170 --> 01:40:38.003
I know.

3338
01:40:38.003 --> 01:40:39.153
I was like, how did this guy have so much energy?

3339
01:40:39.153 --> 01:40:40.153
I just started working it.

3340
01:40:40.153 --> 01:40:42.025
I saw that, I'm like, "Okay, get to it right now

3341
01:40:42.025 --> 01:40:42.858
as fast as you can."

3342
01:40:42.858 --> 01:40:44.821
And I looked at my split laid on my Garmin.

3343
01:40:44.821 --> 01:40:46.816
It was 707 pace at that point

3344
01:40:46.816 --> 01:40:49.991
from running 12 miles in a minute mile to 707.

3345
01:40:49.991 --> 01:40:50.848
That's great, man.

3346
01:40:50.848 --> 01:40:51.681
Yeah, for the last push.

3347
01:40:51.681 --> 01:40:53.609
And how long had you hatched plot

3348
01:40:53.609 --> 01:40:56.275
to pop the question at the finish line?

3349
01:40:56.275 --> 01:40:58.296
I wanted to do it as soon as I started talking

3350
01:40:58.296 --> 01:40:59.694
and thanking everybody and the sponsor,

3351
01:40:59.694 --> 01:41:01.789
everybody for just being there and making this very special.

3352
01:41:01.789 --> 01:41:03.739
So, I told Robbie as soon as I said, "Hey, Robbie,"

3353
01:41:03.739 --> 01:41:04.876
that's when he...

3354
01:41:04.876 --> 01:41:06.110
Robbie had the ring.

3355
01:41:06.110 --> 01:41:07.245
Oh, he did.

3356
01:41:07.245 --> 01:41:08.128
He's the ring bearer.

3357
01:41:08.128 --> 01:41:08.961
Yeah.

3358
01:41:08.961 --> 01:41:09.794
So, I said, "Hey, Robbie."

3359
01:41:09.794 --> 01:41:10.704
He just grabbed it

3360
01:41:10.704 --> 01:41:14.516
and he actually gave it to a friend of ours, Lex Woodshop.

3361
01:41:14.516 --> 01:41:17.780
She hosted Robbie in New Jersey his last day.

3362
01:41:17.780 --> 01:41:22.306
And she had her running backpack or running vest,

3363
01:41:22.306 --> 01:41:23.461
hydration vest.

3364
01:41:23.461 --> 01:41:24.818
And then Robbie grabbed it from her.

3365
01:41:24.818 --> 01:41:25.651
And then I said, "Hey, Robbie."

3366
01:41:25.651 --> 01:41:27.517
Robbie handed it to me and then I went for it.

3367
01:41:27.517 --> 01:41:28.598
Yeah.

3368
01:41:28.598 --> 01:41:29.487
She was surprised.

3369
01:41:29.487 --> 01:41:31.213
Yeah, she had an idea.

3370
01:41:31.213 --> 01:41:32.226
And actually I was like-

3371
01:41:32.226 --> 01:41:35.151
But how did you hide the ring beforehand,

3372
01:41:35.151 --> 01:41:37.875
so she didn't find it for the whole adventure?

3373
01:41:37.875 --> 01:41:39.226
I didn't even have the ring with me.

3374
01:41:39.226 --> 01:41:40.453
Oh was it in in New Jersey

3375
01:41:40.453 --> 01:41:41.758
you had a friend get it or something?

3376
01:41:41.758 --> 01:41:44.469
No, I was trying to figure how I was gonna do this.

3377
01:41:44.469 --> 01:41:46.156
And I called my guardian

3378
01:41:46.156 --> 01:41:48.464
who came to see me a few days before.

3379
01:41:48.464 --> 01:41:50.277
I said, "I was just letting you guys know

3380
01:41:50.277 --> 01:41:51.578
I'm gonna propose to the Lex.

3381
01:41:51.578 --> 01:41:53.072
And I just want you guys know ahead of time

3382
01:41:53.072 --> 01:41:54.534
since I won't see you before."

3383
01:41:54.534 --> 01:41:56.347
And then he goes, "Do you have a ring?"

3384
01:41:56.347 --> 01:41:57.180
I was like, "No."

3385
01:41:57.180 --> 01:41:58.013
He goes, "All right."

3386
01:41:58.013 --> 01:42:00.530
He drove to a jeweler and FaceTime me and said,

3387
01:42:00.530 --> 01:42:01.363
"Hey, can you pick one?"

3388
01:42:01.363 --> 01:42:03.433
I said, "Well, I want it to be unique."

3389
01:42:03.433 --> 01:42:05.206
And so, we did a deal with a jeweler

3390
01:42:05.206 --> 01:42:07.805
where we can pick the ring now and she doesn't like it

3391
01:42:07.805 --> 01:42:10.175
or the fitting is not right, we can go and fix it.

3392
01:42:10.175 --> 01:42:11.517
So, just to have a ring.

3393
01:42:11.517 --> 01:42:12.645
It was either that,

3394
01:42:12.645 --> 01:42:13.934
or I was gonna ask her mom for grandmother's ring,

3395
01:42:13.934 --> 01:42:15.841
who had passed if she had one in person.

3396
01:42:15.841 --> 01:42:17.544
So, I wanted to ask everybody.

3397
01:42:17.544 --> 01:42:18.801
And I didn't even ask the mother yet

3398
01:42:18.801 --> 01:42:21.004
till the day before that I'm gonna propose.

3399
01:42:21.004 --> 01:42:22.585
I asked her father the morning,

3400
01:42:22.585 --> 01:42:24.307
'cause I didn't see him until then.

3401
01:42:24.307 --> 01:42:27.568
So, she saw me talking to these people, like close people

3402
01:42:27.568 --> 01:42:28.676
and I didn't want her to be like,

3403
01:42:28.676 --> 01:42:30.249
"Why is Hellah doing that?"

3404
01:42:30.249 --> 01:42:32.177
So, I would take my GoPro and say,

3405
01:42:32.177 --> 01:42:33.663
"I wanna interview people."

3406
01:42:33.663 --> 01:42:35.102
I interviewed her best friend,

3407
01:42:35.102 --> 01:42:37.502
but I told her best friend while I was doing the interview.

3408
01:42:37.502 --> 01:42:40.768
And then so for her to even fall for the interview thing,

3409
01:42:40.768 --> 01:42:43.476
I called her over, "Now time to interview you now."

3410
01:42:43.476 --> 01:42:44.356
So, I interviewed her too.

3411
01:42:44.356 --> 01:42:46.392
So, she was like, "Oh, he's just interviewing everybody."

3412
01:42:46.392 --> 01:42:47.651
But I was telling people that I'm gonna propose,

3413
01:42:47.651 --> 01:42:49.554
so they're there at the finish line.

3414
01:42:49.554 --> 01:42:50.958
So, that's how I had to set up.

3415
01:42:50.958 --> 01:42:52.280
How long have you guys been together?

3416
01:42:52.280 --> 01:42:54.582
Nine years this past June 11th.

3417
01:42:54.582 --> 01:42:55.415
It was nine years.

3418
01:42:55.415 --> 01:42:57.998
I met her at UMass, in college UMass Emerson.

3419
01:42:57.998 --> 01:42:58.831
Oh, it goes way back.

3420
01:42:58.831 --> 01:43:00.360
Yeah. Yeah.

3421
01:43:00.360 --> 01:43:01.483
Nine years ago.

3422
01:43:01.483 --> 01:43:02.316
Wow. Wow.

3423
01:43:02.316 --> 01:43:03.161
Yeah, it's incredible.

3424
01:43:03.161 --> 01:43:04.405
It flew by too really bad.

3425
01:43:04.405 --> 01:43:06.042
That was the fastest nine years.

3426
01:43:06.042 --> 01:43:09.263
That was the biggest party finish line

3427
01:43:09.263 --> 01:43:11.001
for a run across America that ever was.

3428
01:43:11.001 --> 01:43:12.095
I don't even know.

3429
01:43:12.095 --> 01:43:14.164
Yeah, and Gymshark really went all out for them

3430
01:43:14.164 --> 01:43:16.105
to get that and then getting a permit for the road

3431
01:43:16.105 --> 01:43:18.961
for us to get the finish line on.

3432
01:43:18.961 --> 01:43:20.115
And it was just really fun.

3433
01:43:20.115 --> 01:43:23.247
And it was even more exciting to have Casey Neistat there,

3434
01:43:23.247 --> 01:43:25.730
to have Robbie, just everybody that-

3435
01:43:25.730 --> 01:43:27.012
How did that come together?

3436
01:43:27.012 --> 01:43:30.271
Okay, so Gymshark asked me actually,

3437
01:43:30.271 --> 01:43:31.945
"Hellah, who do you want at the start of your run

3438
01:43:31.945 --> 01:43:32.778
across the country?"

3439
01:43:32.778 --> 01:43:35.130
I said, "Rich Roll, Casey Neistat."

3440
01:43:35.130 --> 01:43:35.963
You two-

3441
01:43:35.963 --> 01:43:36.796
I didn't know.

3442
01:43:36.796 --> 01:43:37.629
Nobody told me.

3443
01:43:37.629 --> 01:43:39.431
I'm shocked actually, because they asked me.

3444
01:43:39.431 --> 01:43:41.703
They said, "Hellah, is there anybody important

3445
01:43:41.703 --> 01:43:44.859
that you really look up to or you want at your start?"

3446
01:43:44.859 --> 01:43:47.001
You two were the first in my head immediately.

3447
01:43:47.001 --> 01:43:48.149
I had no idea.

3448
01:43:48.149 --> 01:43:49.358
I knew Robbie was gonna-

3449
01:43:49.358 --> 01:43:50.425
I would've joined you for the beginning.

3450
01:43:50.425 --> 01:43:52.284
Yeah, I knew Robbie would have came.

3451
01:43:52.284 --> 01:43:53.524
Robbie was, I talked to Robbie.

3452
01:43:53.524 --> 01:43:55.485
Robbie, said, "Hellah, I'm there for you as a friend.

3453
01:43:55.485 --> 01:43:56.720
I'm gonna be there for you."

3454
01:43:56.720 --> 01:43:57.740
So, I knew he was doing his thing.

3455
01:43:57.740 --> 01:43:59.074
Eventually, I was gonna meet Robbie somewhere,

3456
01:43:59.074 --> 01:44:00.369
even if it's the finish.

3457
01:44:00.369 --> 01:44:02.638
So, they asked me and I said you two immediately.

3458
01:44:02.638 --> 01:44:05.007
Many times and many meetings, we have Zoom meetings.

3459
01:44:05.007 --> 01:44:05.840
And so, I thought-

3460
01:44:05.840 --> 01:44:08.181
I think there were emails that came in that I didn't see

3461
01:44:08.181 --> 01:44:09.342
or didn't pay attention to.

3462
01:44:09.342 --> 01:44:10.175
Now I feel bad.

3463
01:44:10.175 --> 01:44:11.008
No, that's all right,

3464
01:44:11.008 --> 01:44:12.504
because I'm sitting here now with you. (laughs)

3465
01:44:12.504 --> 01:44:13.673
But I've mentioned you two.

3466
01:44:13.673 --> 01:44:14.522
And then the same thing

3467
01:44:14.522 --> 01:44:17.741
and none of that has happened in the beginning.

3468
01:44:17.741 --> 01:44:19.511
I didn't see either of you.

3469
01:44:19.511 --> 01:44:22.547
So, but in the finish, as I'm finishing, I was asked again,

3470
01:44:22.547 --> 01:44:23.881
"Who do you want at to finish last day?"

3471
01:44:23.881 --> 01:44:25.907
Rich Roll and Casey.

3472
01:44:25.907 --> 01:44:27.704
And those are some of the people I said.

3473
01:44:27.704 --> 01:44:28.800
I definitely didn't know about that.

3474
01:44:28.800 --> 01:44:30.123
But I completely forgot about it.

3475
01:44:30.123 --> 01:44:33.354
Like to a point, I was just so consumed, just get home.

3476
01:44:33.354 --> 01:44:34.597
And then I see Casey the next morning.

3477
01:44:34.597 --> 01:44:36.529
I'm like, "Whoa, Casey is actually here?"

3478
01:44:36.529 --> 01:44:38.554
But I had no idea he was gonna show up.

3479
01:44:38.554 --> 01:44:39.532
So, to me too,

3480
01:44:39.532 --> 01:44:41.515
they were just asking me if I can have somebody,

3481
01:44:41.515 --> 01:44:42.457
maybe they'll try it.

3482
01:44:42.457 --> 01:44:43.716
That was gonna be like high happened in the beginning.

3483
01:44:43.716 --> 01:44:45.458
And I knew you guys are busy.

3484
01:44:45.458 --> 01:44:47.353
It was just that to me when they asked me,

3485
01:44:47.353 --> 01:44:49.290
"Who do you think, if you can pick anybody?"

3486
01:44:49.290 --> 01:44:50.689
That's my answer.

3487
01:44:50.689 --> 01:44:51.627
It was you two.

3488
01:44:51.627 --> 01:44:52.460
Yeah.

3489
01:44:52.460 --> 01:44:54.580
Well, I can tell you that when I was watching it

3490
01:44:54.580 --> 01:44:56.973
unfold on Instagram, I was like, "Why am I not there?"

3491
01:44:56.973 --> 01:44:59.343
I was like, I had huge FOMO.

3492
01:44:59.343 --> 01:45:00.618
I was like, I should be there.

3493
01:45:00.618 --> 01:45:01.760
Everyone is there.

3494
01:45:01.760 --> 01:45:02.868
This looks like so much fun.

3495
01:45:02.868 --> 01:45:03.701
I can't-

3496
01:45:03.701 --> 01:45:04.737
Maybe I should have tried to reach out to you.

3497
01:45:04.737 --> 01:45:06.699
I should have DMed you have him do and say,

3498
01:45:06.699 --> 01:45:08.133
"Hey, Rich, can you come out too?"

3499
01:45:08.133 --> 01:45:09.739
Well, you're here now.

3500
01:45:09.739 --> 01:45:11.219
You're here now.

3501
01:45:11.219 --> 01:45:13.902
I feel like you should also go to Mali

3502
01:45:13.902 --> 01:45:15.038
and take a victory lap.

3503
01:45:15.038 --> 01:45:16.534
They probably started your parade there.

3504
01:45:16.534 --> 01:45:17.755
I definitely wanna do that.

3505
01:45:17.755 --> 01:45:19.526
I'm thinking like around end of the year,

3506
01:45:19.526 --> 01:45:20.359
December I go to Mali.

3507
01:45:20.359 --> 01:45:21.263
That would be cool.

3508
01:45:21.263 --> 01:45:22.096
Yeah. Yeah.

3509
01:45:22.096 --> 01:45:22.997
You could make an amazing video out of that too.

3510
01:45:22.997 --> 01:45:24.829
Yeah, I'm looking forward to going back home.

3511
01:45:24.829 --> 01:45:26.812
'Cause I haven't been there since 2018.

3512
01:45:26.812 --> 01:45:28.118
So, it's been some time.

3513
01:45:28.118 --> 01:45:30.721
It would also be cool to a video with Buddy

3514
01:45:30.721 --> 01:45:33.454
and track like the money that you raised

3515
01:45:33.454 --> 01:45:37.831
and kind of help tell the Soles4Souls story

3516
01:45:37.831 --> 01:45:42.635
and maybe see what kind of impact is being made in Mali.

3517
01:45:42.635 --> 01:45:44.863
Wow, you just gave me a great idea.

3518
01:45:44.863 --> 01:45:45.696
Yeah, man.

3519
01:45:45.696 --> 01:45:46.529
Yeah.

3520
01:45:46.529 --> 01:45:47.362
You're a content creator now.

3521
01:45:47.362 --> 01:45:48.195
Yeah, there you go.

3522
01:45:48.195 --> 01:45:49.028
Full time, full stop.

3523
01:45:49.028 --> 01:45:49.861
Yeah, that is it.

3524
01:45:49.861 --> 01:45:50.694
There's no way back.

3525
01:45:50.694 --> 01:45:51.527
There's not turning around.

3526
01:45:51.527 --> 01:45:52.360
Just going at it.

3527
01:45:52.360 --> 01:45:53.454
Yeah, from now on.

3528
01:45:53.454 --> 01:45:54.541
Well, before I let you go,

3529
01:45:54.541 --> 01:45:57.648
I think it would be good to kind of pivot a little bit

3530
01:45:57.648 --> 01:46:01.898
to talk about have a change and staying motivated.

3531
01:46:05.216 --> 01:46:07.321
What you've done is so inspirational.

3532
01:46:07.321 --> 01:46:10.040
And I feel like you do such a good job

3533
01:46:10.040 --> 01:46:13.633
at communicating these ideas in a relatable way.

3534
01:46:13.633 --> 01:46:16.068
So, for the people that are watching or listening

3535
01:46:16.068 --> 01:46:18.732
who are feeling inspired

3536
01:46:18.732 --> 01:46:21.917
and know they need to get off the couch and do something,

3537
01:46:21.917 --> 01:46:23.872
it doesn't necessarily have to be a run streak,

3538
01:46:23.872 --> 01:46:26.261
but perhaps, are in the process

3539
01:46:26.261 --> 01:46:29.033
of rethinking their relationship to their body

3540
01:46:29.033 --> 01:46:32.259
and their selves and the trajectory that they're on in life,

3541
01:46:32.259 --> 01:46:33.566
like how do you speak to that person?

3542
01:46:33.566 --> 01:46:36.934
I always say, do something that's pressure-free

3543
01:46:36.934 --> 01:46:39.195
and do something that's attainable.

3544
01:46:39.195 --> 01:46:41.296
Always those are the biggest factor for me.

3545
01:46:41.296 --> 01:46:42.727
And pressure-free, meaning, don't do it

3546
01:46:42.727 --> 01:46:45.757
because someone else is doing it,

3547
01:46:45.757 --> 01:46:48.679
do it because you wanna do it and do it on your own timing.

3548
01:46:48.679 --> 01:46:50.267
Don't feel you gotta get it done.

3549
01:46:50.267 --> 01:46:51.599
If it's a goal, whatever,

3550
01:46:51.599 --> 01:46:53.511
you don't have to get it done in 10 days,

3551
01:46:53.511 --> 01:46:55.244
if you need a month, a month is okay.

3552
01:46:55.244 --> 01:46:56.771
So, just do it pressure-free.

3553
01:46:56.771 --> 01:46:59.114
Because of that, I fell in love with running.

3554
01:46:59.114 --> 01:47:00.488
I never thought it was no chance.

3555
01:47:00.488 --> 01:47:01.935
And now I get excited to run.

3556
01:47:01.935 --> 01:47:03.226
And I know running is tough.

3557
01:47:03.226 --> 01:47:04.680
It has it's brutal days,

3558
01:47:04.680 --> 01:47:07.071
but like I'm still excited to go at it.

3559
01:47:07.071 --> 01:47:07.904
So, do it-

3560
01:47:07.904 --> 01:47:09.875
You don't feel the pressure of maintaining the streak.

3561
01:47:09.875 --> 01:47:10.796
Nope, zero pressure.

3562
01:47:10.796 --> 01:47:12.078
And I always say this too.

3563
01:47:12.078 --> 01:47:13.771
This is how I feel about it.

3564
01:47:13.771 --> 01:47:16.523
The day that I feel like it becomes more of a pressure

3565
01:47:16.523 --> 01:47:18.936
and I'm not liking it, I'm gonna stop.

3566
01:47:18.936 --> 01:47:19.769
I'll stop.

3567
01:47:19.769 --> 01:47:20.841
And then I don't know when that day is.

3568
01:47:20.841 --> 01:47:21.945
Give yourself that permission.

3569
01:47:21.945 --> 01:47:22.778
Yeah. Yeah.

3570
01:47:22.778 --> 01:47:24.719
And I know I'll find something else.

3571
01:47:24.719 --> 01:47:25.552
I'll find something else.

3572
01:47:25.552 --> 01:47:27.532
So, making sure it's not,

3573
01:47:27.532 --> 01:47:28.552
I don't have to go,

3574
01:47:28.552 --> 01:47:31.395
I know I don't have to go run to keep a streak going,

3575
01:47:31.395 --> 01:47:32.707
but I just do it because it feels good.

3576
01:47:32.707 --> 01:47:34.208
I enjoy it and I wanna keep sharing it.

3577
01:47:34.208 --> 01:47:37.698
So, pressure-free, do it something that's attainable.

3578
01:47:37.698 --> 01:47:40.891
And just think about even spending five minutes a day

3579
01:47:40.891 --> 01:47:42.103
goes a long way.

3580
01:47:42.103 --> 01:47:43.310
If it's something you love already,

3581
01:47:43.310 --> 01:47:44.775
or you're thinking about, you've been thinking about,

3582
01:47:44.775 --> 01:47:46.643
that's the all the sign to start doing it.

3583
01:47:46.643 --> 01:47:47.906
So, if that hadn't just been five minutes a day,

3584
01:47:47.906 --> 01:47:49.806
it's about volume.

3585
01:47:49.806 --> 01:47:52.094
Five minutes a day for seven days a week, it's gonna add up.

3586
01:47:52.094 --> 01:47:55.351
But if you just do it today and you take a few days off,

3587
01:47:55.351 --> 01:47:56.423
that's not it.

3588
01:47:56.423 --> 01:47:58.359
If you can do 10 minutes a day, that's also 10 minutes.

3589
01:47:58.359 --> 01:48:00.020
You can at least find out your day

3590
01:48:00.020 --> 01:48:01.310
if it's important enough to you.

3591
01:48:01.310 --> 01:48:04.215
So, as long as you wanna do it and just pressure-free

3592
01:48:04.215 --> 01:48:05.048
and get after it.

3593
01:48:05.048 --> 01:48:06.750
And don't think about anybody.

3594
01:48:06.750 --> 01:48:07.583
Even don't compare.

3595
01:48:07.583 --> 01:48:09.600
Even if it's running, don't compare yourself to these people

3596
01:48:09.600 --> 01:48:11.162
who are doing hundreds of miles,

